#: data\json\furniture_and_terrain\furniture-appliances.json
msgid "An advanced butchering station connected to a electrical grid."
msgstr "전력망에 연결된 고급 도축 작업대입니다."

#: data\json\furniture_and_terrain\furniture-appliances.json
#: data\json\items\fake.json
msgid "grid hydraulic press"
msgid_plural "grid hydraulic presss"
msgstr[0] "전력망 유압 프레스"

#. ~ Description for grid hydraulic press
#. ~ Description for {'str': 'mounted hydraulic press'}
#: data\json\furniture_and_terrain\furniture-appliances.json
#: data\json\vehicleparts\crafting.json
msgid ""
"If you really want to squash something a lot, this would be exactly the "
"right industrial tool for you."
msgstr "무언가를 정말 많이 찌부러뜨리고 싶다면, 이것이 바로 당신에게 딱 맞는 산업용 도구입니다."

#: data\json\furniture_and_terrain\furniture-appliances.json
#: data\json\furniture_and_terrain\terrain-manufactured.json
#: data\json\items\furniture.json
msgid "metal compactor"
msgid_plural "metal compactors"
msgstr[0] "금속 압축기"

#. ~ Description for metal compactor
#: data\json\furniture_and_terrain\furniture-appliances.json
#: data\json\furniture_and_terrain\terrain-manufactured.json
msgid ""
"A hydraulic compactor that can accept items made of various metals, and "
"press them into basic shapes, ready for further crafting.  If you're very "
"careful, you can even uninstall it to transport it elsewhere."
msgstr ""
"다양한 금속으로 된 아이템을 넣어 기본 형태로 압축해 추가 제작에 쓸 수 있게 하는 유압 압축기입니다. 매우 조심한다면 다른 곳으로 "
"옮기기 위해 분해할 수도 있습니다."

#: data\json\furniture_and_terrain\furniture-appliances.json
#: data\json\furniture_and_terrain\terrain-manufactured.json
#: data\json\items\vehicle\utilities.json
msgid "cloning vat"
msgid_plural "cloning vats"
msgstr[0] "복제용 원통"

#. ~ Description for cloning vat
#: data\json\furniture_and_terrain\furniture-appliances.json
msgid ""
"A vat full of solution, probably intended to hold growing clones of people "
"or other life forms.  Requires a steady, strong power supply to avoid "
"failure.  Examine it to activate, requires a sterile artificial womb and "
"viable DNA, the latter produced via a genome workstation from stored sample "
"data off USB and sufficient growth medium."
msgstr ""
"사람이나 다른 생명체의 성장하는 클론을 담아두기 위한 용액이 가득한 통입니다. 실패를 막으려면 안정적이고 강력한 전원 공급이 필요합니다."
" 조사하면 활성화됩니다. 무균 인공 자궁과 생존 가능한 DNA가 필요하며, 후자는 USB에 저장된 샘플 데이터와 충분한 성장 배지로 게놈"
" 워크스테이션에서 생산합니다."

#: data\json\furniture_and_terrain\furniture-appliances.json
#: data\json\furniture_and_terrain\terrain-fences-gates.json
#: data\json\furniture_and_terrain\terrain-manufactured.json
msgid "ker-rash!"
msgstr "쨍-그랑!"

#: data\json\furniture_and_terrain\furniture-appliances.json
#: data\json\furniture_and_terrain\terrain-manufactured.json
msgid "plunk."
msgstr "쿵."

#: data\json\furniture_and_terrain\furniture-appliances.json
msgid "active cloning vat"
msgstr "활성화된 클론 배양통"

#. ~ Description for active cloning vat
#: data\json\furniture_and_terrain\furniture-appliances.json
msgid ""
"A vat full of solution, its surface rippling as bubbles rise to the top.  It"
" hums softly, the liquid churning as if something inside is taking shape."
msgstr ""
"용액이 가득한 통으로, 거품이 위로 올라오며 표면이 물결칩니다. 안에서 무언가가 형태를 갖추는 듯 액체가 휘저어지며, 조용히 윙윙거리고 "
"있습니다."

#: data\json\furniture_and_terrain\furniture-appliances.json
#: data\json\items\fake.json
msgid "grid basic analysis kit"
msgid_plural "grid basic analysis kits"
msgstr[0] "전력망 기본 분석 키트"

#. ~ Description for grid basic analysis kit
#: data\json\furniture_and_terrain\furniture-appliances.json
msgid ""
"A basic laboratory analysis kit connected to an electrical grid, drawing "
"power instead of batteries.  Its spectrophotometer, pH meter, and other "
"instruments work just as well as the portable version."
msgstr ""
"배터리 대신 전력망에서 전력을 끌어쓰는, 전력망에 연결된 기본 실험실 분석 키트입니다. 분광광도계, pH 측정기 등의 기기는 휴대용만큼 "
"잘 작동합니다."

#: data\json\furniture_and_terrain\furniture-appliances.json
#: data\json\items\fake.json
msgid "grid microcentrifuge"
msgid_plural "grid microcentrifuges"
msgstr[0] "전력망 소형 원심분리기"

#. ~ Description for grid microcentrifuge
#: data\json\furniture_and_terrain\furniture-appliances.json
msgid ""
"A microcentrifuge connected to an electrical grid, drawing power instead of "
"batteries.  Bench-sized but still very fast."
msgstr "배터리 대신 전력망에서 전력을 끌어쓰는, 전력망에 연결된 소형 원심분리기입니다. 실험대 크기지만 여전히 매우 빠릅니다."

#: data\json\furniture_and_terrain\furniture-appliances.json
#: data\json\items\fake.json
msgid "grid genome workstation"
msgid_plural "grid genome workstations"
msgstr[0] "전력망 게놈 워크스테이션"

#. ~ Description for grid genome workstation
#: data\json\furniture_and_terrain\furniture-appliances.json
msgid ""
"A genome workstation connected to an electrical grid, drawing power instead "
"of batteries.  Can scan genetic samples and produce DNA samples for cloning."
msgstr ""
"배터리 대신 전력망에서 전력을 끌어쓰는, 전력망에 연결된 게놈 워크스테이션입니다. 유전 샘플을 스캔하고 클론 제작용 DNA 샘플을 생산할"
" 수 있습니다."

#: data\json\furniture_and_terrain\furniture-barriers.json
msgid "road barricade"
msgstr "도로 바리케이드"

#. ~ Description for road barricade
#: data\json\furniture_and_terrain\furniture-barriers.json
msgid ""
"A road barricade.  For barricading roads.  You could stand next to it to "
"fire past without it blocking your shots, not that it will slow them down "
"much."
msgstr ""
"도로 바리케이드입니다. 도로를 막기 위한 것입니다. 옆에 서서 넘겨서 사격하면 발사를 막지 않지만, 그렇다고 적을 크게 지연시키지는 "
"못합니다."

#: data\json\furniture_and_terrain\furniture-barriers.json
msgid "simple wooden barricade"
msgstr "단순한 목재 바리케이드"

#. ~ Description for simple wooden barricade
#: data\json\furniture_and_terrain\furniture-barriers.json
msgid ""
"A waist-high barricade made of stout saplings, held in place by poles "
"hammered into the ground.  Useful to fence in a campsite and shelter a fire "
"from the wind, or slow down intruders."
msgstr ""
"땅에 박은 기둥으로 고정된, 굵은 묘목으로 만든 허리 높이 바리케이드입니다. 야영지에 울타리를 두르고 불을 바람에서 보호하거나 침입자를 "
"지연시키는 데 유용합니다."

#: data\json\furniture_and_terrain\furniture-barriers.json
msgid "earthbag barricade"
msgstr "흙자루 바리케이드"

#. ~ Description for earthbag barricade
#: data\json\furniture_and_terrain\furniture-barriers.json
msgid ""
"An earthbag barricade, typically used for blocking bullets.  Stand next to "
"it to fire past it unimpeded."
msgstr "주로 총알을 막는 데 쓰이는 흙자루 바리케이드입니다. 옆에 서서 넘겨서 방해받지 않고 사격할 수 있습니다."

#: data\json\furniture_and_terrain\furniture-barriers.json
msgid "rrrip!"
msgstr "찌이이익!"

#: data\json\furniture_and_terrain\furniture-barriers.json
msgid "earthbag wall"
msgstr "흙자루 벽"

#. ~ Description for earthbag wall
#: data\json\furniture_and_terrain\furniture-barriers.json
msgid "An earthbag wall."
msgstr "흙자루 벽입니다."

#: data\json\furniture_and_terrain\furniture-barriers.json
msgid "lane guard"
msgstr "레인가드"

#. ~ Description for lane guard
#: data\json\furniture_and_terrain\furniture-barriers.json
msgid "Used to be used for keeping traffic."
msgstr "예전에 교통 통제에 사용되었습니다."

#: data\json\furniture_and_terrain\furniture-barriers.json
msgid "sandbag barricade"
msgstr "모래주머니 바리케이드"

#. ~ Description for sandbag barricade
#: data\json\furniture_and_terrain\furniture-barriers.json
msgid ""
"A sandbag barricade, typically used for blocking bullets.  Stand next to it "
"to fire past it unimpeded."
msgstr "주로 총알을 막는 데 쓰이는 모래주머니 바리케이드입니다. 옆에 서서 넘겨서 방해받지 않고 사격할 수 있습니다."

#: data\json\furniture_and_terrain\furniture-barriers.json
msgid "sandbag wall"
msgstr "모래주머니 벽"

#. ~ Description for sandbag wall
#: data\json\furniture_and_terrain\furniture-barriers.json
msgid "A sandbag wall."
msgstr "모래주머니 벽입니다."

#: data\json\furniture_and_terrain\furniture-decorative.json
msgid "standing mirror"
msgstr "전신거울"

#. ~ Description for standing mirror
#: data\json\furniture_and_terrain\furniture-decorative.json
msgid ""
"Lookin' good - is that blood?  Examine it to practice the Speech skill and "
"give yourself a pep talk."
msgstr "잘생겼는데 - 저거 피야? 조사하면 대화술 기술을 연습하고 자신에게 격려의 말을 해줄 수 있습니다."

#: data\json\furniture_and_terrain\furniture-decorative.json
#: data\json\furniture_and_terrain\furniture-storage.json
msgid "glass breaking"
msgstr "쨍그랑!"

#: data\json\furniture_and_terrain\furniture-decorative.json
msgid "broken standing mirror"
msgstr "깨진 전신거울"

#. ~ Description for broken standing mirror
#: data\json\furniture_and_terrain\furniture-decorative.json
msgid ""
"You could look at yourself, if the mirror wasn't covered in cracks and "
"fractures."
msgstr "거울이 금과 균열로 뒤덮이지 않았다면 자신을 볼 수 있을 것입니다."

#: data\json\furniture_and_terrain\furniture-decorative.json
msgid "bitts"
msgstr "계류 기둥"

#. ~ Description for bitts
#: data\json\furniture_and_terrain\furniture-decorative.json
msgid ""
"Paired vertical iron posts mounted on a wharf, pier or quay.  They are used "
"to secure mooring lines, ropes, hawsers, or cables."
msgstr "부두·선착장·안벽에 설치된 한 쌍의 수직 철기둥입니다. 계류 로프·밧줄·홋줄·케이블을 고정하는 데 사용됩니다."

#: data\json\furniture_and_terrain\furniture-decorative.json
msgid "cleat"
msgstr "클리트"

#. ~ Description for cleat
#: data\json\furniture_and_terrain\furniture-decorative.json
msgid ""
"A small horn cleat with two “horns” extending parallel to the deck or the "
"axis of the spar, and resembling a small anvil.  They are used to secure "
"mooring lines, ropes, and similar."
msgstr ""
"갑판이나 돛대 축과 평행하게 뻗은 두 개의 '뿔'이 달린 작은 뿔형 클리트로, 작은 모루를 닮았습니다. 계류 로프와 밧줄 등을 고정하는 "
"데 사용됩니다."

#: data\json\furniture_and_terrain\furniture-decorative.json
msgid "manacles"
msgstr "족쇄"

#. ~ Description for manacles
#: data\json\furniture_and_terrain\furniture-decorative.json
msgid ""
"Chain serfs in your dungeon.  All you need now is an iron ball to chain to "
"it."
msgstr "던전에 농노를 묶어두세요. 이제 필요한 건 여기에 묶을 쇠구슬뿐입니다."

#: data\json\furniture_and_terrain\furniture-decorative.json
#: data\json\furniture_and_terrain\furniture-domestic_plants.json
#: data\json\furniture_and_terrain\terrain-doors.json
#: data\json\furniture_and_terrain\terrain-fences-gates.json
#: data\json\furniture_and_terrain\terrain-railroads.json
msgid "crack."
msgstr "콰직."

#: data\json\furniture_and_terrain\furniture-decorative.json
msgid "statue"
msgstr "동상"

#. ~ Description for statue
#: data\json\furniture_and_terrain\furniture-decorative.json
msgid "A carved statue made of stone."
msgstr "돌로 조각된 석상입니다."

#: data\json\furniture_and_terrain\furniture-decorative.json
#: data\json\furniture_and_terrain\furniture-graves.json
#: data\json\furniture_and_terrain\furniture-rural.json
#: data\json\furniture_and_terrain\furniture-terrains.json
#: data\mods\Arcana_BN\furniture_and_terrain\furniture.json
#: data\mods\MagicalNights\furniture.json
#: data\mods\desert_region\desert_terrain.json
msgid "thump."
msgstr "쿵."

#: data\json\furniture_and_terrain\furniture-decorative.json
msgid "mannequin"
msgstr "마네킹"

#. ~ Description for mannequin
#: data\json\furniture_and_terrain\furniture-decorative.json
msgid ""
"Put clothes on it, talk to it.  Who's around to judge you?  Wait… did it "
"just move?  Assuming it doesn't talk back, could be used to practice the "
"Speech skill."
msgstr ""
"옷을 입히고 말을 걸어보세요. 누가 판단할 사람이 있기나 한가요? 잠깐… 방금 움직인 건가? 말대꾸하지 않는다는 전제로, 대화술 기술을 "
"연습하는 데 쓸 수 있습니다."

#: data\json\furniture_and_terrain\furniture-decorative.json
msgid "birdbath"
msgstr "새 목욕통"

#. ~ Description for birdbath
#: data\json\furniture_and_terrain\furniture-decorative.json
msgid "A decorative cement birdbath and pedestal."
msgstr "장식용 시멘트 새 목욕통과 받침대입니다."

#: data\json\furniture_and_terrain\furniture-decorative.json
msgid "rotary clothes dryer line"
msgstr "회전식 빨래 건조대"

#. ~ Description for rotary clothes dryer line
#: data\json\furniture_and_terrain\furniture-decorative.json
msgid "A umbrella shaped clothes line mounted on a pole."
msgstr "기둥에 설치된 우산 모양 빨랫줄입니다."

#: data\json\furniture_and_terrain\furniture-decorative.json
msgid "pine wreath"
msgstr "소나무 리스"

#. ~ Description for pine wreath
#: data\json\furniture_and_terrain\furniture-decorative.json
msgid "A decorative wreath for the winter holidays."
msgstr "겨울 명절용 장식 리스입니다."

#: data\json\furniture_and_terrain\furniture-decorative.json
msgid "decorative tree"
msgstr "장식용 나무"

#. ~ Description for decorative tree
#: data\json\furniture_and_terrain\furniture-decorative.json
msgid "A decorative tree for the winter holidays."
msgstr "겨울 명절용 장식 나무입니다."

#: data\json\furniture_and_terrain\furniture-dim-portals.json
#: data\json\furniture_and_terrain\terrain-nether.json
msgid "dimensional portal"
msgstr "차원 포탈"

#. ~ Description for dimensional portal
#: data\json\furniture_and_terrain\furniture-dim-portals.json
msgid ""
"A shimmering aperture in space, held open by an arcane-industrial framework."
" Unlinked."
msgstr "비전 산업 골조로 열려 있는, 공간에 아른거리는 틈새입니다. 미연결."

#: data\json\furniture_and_terrain\furniture-dim-portals.json
msgid "a resonant crack!"
msgstr "공명하는 파열 소리!"

#: data\json\furniture_and_terrain\furniture-dim-portals.json
msgid "dimensional portal (active)"
msgstr "차원 포탈 (활성)"

#. ~ Description for dimensional portal (active)
#: data\json\furniture_and_terrain\furniture-dim-portals.json
msgid ""
"A shimmering aperture in space, held open by an arcane-industrial framework."
" Examining it will transport you to the linked dimension."
msgstr "비전 산업 골조로 열려 있는, 공간에 아른거리는 틈새입니다. 조사하면 연결된 차원으로 이동됩니다."

#: data\json\furniture_and_terrain\furniture-dim-portals.json
msgid "dimensional portal (closed)"
msgstr "차원 포탈 (닫힘)"

#. ~ Description for dimensional portal (closed)
#: data\json\furniture_and_terrain\furniture-dim-portals.json
msgid ""
"The arcane-industrial framework of a dimensional portal, its aperture now "
"sealed. The dimensional connection it once maintained has collapsed."
msgstr "차원 포탈의 비전 산업 골조로, 틈새는 이제 봉인되었습니다. 한때 유지되던 차원 연결이 붕괴했습니다."

#: data\json\furniture_and_terrain\furniture-dim-portals.json
msgid "power portal"
msgstr "전력 포탈"

#. ~ Description for power portal
#: data\json\furniture_and_terrain\furniture-dim-portals.json
msgid ""
"A large arcane-industrial apparatus that can form a persistent electrical "
"bridge to a paired node, even across dimensional boundaries. Unlinked."
msgstr "차원 경계를 넘어서도 한 쌍의 노드에 지속적인 전기 다리를 형성할 수 있는 대형 비전 산업 장치입니다. 미연결."

#: data\json\furniture_and_terrain\furniture-dim-portals.json
msgid "power portal (active)"
msgstr "전력 포탈 (활성)"

#. ~ Description for power portal (active)
#: data\json\furniture_and_terrain\furniture-dim-portals.json
msgid ""
"A large arcane-industrial apparatus forming a persistent electrical bridge "
"to a paired node. The hum of power flowing through the dimensional membrane "
"is faintly audible."
msgstr ""
"한 쌍의 노드에 지속적인 전기 다리를 형성하는 대형 비전 산업 장치입니다. 차원막을 통해 흐르는 전력의 윙윙거림이 희미하게 들립니다."

#: data\json\furniture_and_terrain\furniture-dim-portals.json
msgid "power portal (paused)"
msgstr "전력 포탈 (일시정지)"

#. ~ Description for power portal (paused)
#: data\json\furniture_and_terrain\furniture-dim-portals.json
msgid ""
"A large arcane-industrial apparatus configured to form an electrical bridge,"
" but currently inactive due to insufficient power or a manual pause."
msgstr "전기 다리를 형성하도록 설정된 대형 비전 산업 장치이지만, 전력 부족이나 수동 일시정지로 현재 비활성 상태입니다."

#: data\json\furniture_and_terrain\furniture-domestic_plants.json
msgid "indoor plant"
msgstr "실내 조경식물"

#. ~ Description for indoor plant
#: data\json\furniture_and_terrain\furniture-domestic_plants.json
msgid "A variety of plant, used for decoration."
msgstr "장식용으로 사용되는 다양한 식물입니다."

#: data\json\furniture_and_terrain\furniture-domestic_plants.json
msgid "yellow indoor plant"
msgstr "노란 실내 조경식물"

#. ~ Description for yellow indoor plant
#: data\json\furniture_and_terrain\furniture-domestic_plants.json
msgid "A variety of plant for decoration.  It's yellow."
msgstr "장식을 위한 식물. 노랗다."

#: data\json\furniture_and_terrain\furniture-domestic_plants.json
msgid "harvestable plant"
msgstr "수확 가능 작물"

#. ~ Description for harvestable plant
#: data\json\furniture_and_terrain\furniture-domestic_plants.json
msgid ""
"This plant is ready for harvest.  Examine it more closely to identify how to"
" harvest the plant appropriately."
msgstr "수확 준비가 된 식물입니다. 더 자세히 조사하면 적절한 수확 방법을 알아낼 수 있습니다."

#: data\json\furniture_and_terrain\furniture-domestic_plants.json
#: data\json\furniture_and_terrain\furniture-flora.json
#: data\json\furniture_and_terrain\furniture-terrains.json
#: data\json\furniture_and_terrain\terrain-flora.json
#: data\json\furniture_and_terrain\terrain-fungal.json
#: data\json\furniture_and_terrain\terrain-manufactured.json
#: data\json\furniture_and_terrain\terrain-triffid.json
#: data\mods\desert_region\desert_terrain.json
msgid "crunch."
msgstr "우지끈."

#: data\json\furniture_and_terrain\furniture-domestic_plants.json
#: data\json\furniture_and_terrain\furniture-flora.json
#: data\json\furniture_and_terrain\furniture-rural.json
#: data\json\furniture_and_terrain\terrain-flora.json
msgid "whish."
msgstr "쉬잇."

#: data\json\furniture_and_terrain\furniture-domestic_plants.json
msgid "maturing plant"
msgstr "성장 중인 식물"

#. ~ Description for maturing plant
#: data\json\furniture_and_terrain\furniture-domestic_plants.json
msgid "This plant is maturing."
msgstr "이 식물은 성장 중입니다."

#: data\json\furniture_and_terrain\furniture-domestic_plants.json
#: src/iuse_actor.cpp
msgid "seed"
msgstr "씨앗"

#. ~ Description for seed
#: data\json\furniture_and_terrain\furniture-domestic_plants.json
msgid ""
"A humble planted seed.  Actions are the seed of fate deeds grow into "
"destiny."
msgstr "심어진 소박한 씨앗입니다. 행동은 운명의 씨앗이고, 행적은 숙명으로 자라납니다."

#: data\json\furniture_and_terrain\furniture-domestic_plants.json
#: src/iuse_actor.cpp
msgid "seedling"
msgstr "묘목"

#. ~ Description for seedling
#: data\json\furniture_and_terrain\furniture-domestic_plants.json
msgid "This plant is just getting started."
msgstr "이 식물은 이제 막 자라기 시작했습니다."

#: data\json\furniture_and_terrain\furniture-domestic_plants.json
msgid "planter"
msgstr "파종기"

#. ~ Description for planter
#: data\json\furniture_and_terrain\furniture-domestic_plants.json
msgid ""
"A garden planter full of soil and slatted to allow adequate drainage.  Can "
"be used for planting crops."
msgstr "흙이 가득 담기고 배수가 잘 되도록 판자로 된 정원 화분대입니다. 작물을 심는 데 쓸 수 있습니다."

#: data\json\furniture_and_terrain\furniture-domestic_plants.json
msgid "planter with harvestable plant"
msgstr "수확 가능한 식물이 든 화분대"

#. ~ Description for planter with harvestable plant
#. ~ Description for planter with maturing plant
#. ~ Description for planter with seed
#: data\json\furniture_and_terrain\furniture-domestic_plants.json
msgid ""
"A garden planter full of soil and slatted to allow adequate drainage.  Can "
"be used for planting crops.  This one contains a planted seed"
msgstr ""
"흙이 가득 담기고 배수가 잘 되도록 판자로 된 정원 화분대입니다. 작물을 심는 데 쓸 수 있습니다. 이것에는 심어진 씨앗이 있습니다."

#: data\json\furniture_and_terrain\furniture-domestic_plants.json
msgid "planter with maturing plant"
msgstr "성장 중인 식물이 든 화분대"

#: data\json\furniture_and_terrain\furniture-domestic_plants.json
msgid "planter with seed"
msgstr "씨앗이 든 화분대"

#: data\json\furniture_and_terrain\furniture-domestic_plants.json
msgid "planter with seedling"
msgstr "모종이 든 화분대"

#. ~ Description for planter with seedling
#: data\json\furniture_and_terrain\furniture-domestic_plants.json
msgid ""
"A garden planter full of soil and slatted to allow adequate drainage.  Can "
"be used for planting crops.  This one contains a planted seedling"
msgstr ""
"흙이 가득 담기고 배수가 잘 되도록 판자로 된 정원 화분대입니다. 작물을 심는 데 쓸 수 있습니다. 이것에는 심어진 모종이 있습니다."

#: data\json\furniture_and_terrain\furniture-domestic_plants.json
msgid "mushroom rack"
msgstr "버섯 재배 선반"

#. ~ Description for mushroom rack
#: data\json\furniture_and_terrain\furniture-domestic_plants.json
msgid ""
"A rack specifically made for raising mushrooms.  You can plant mushroom "
"cultures in here."
msgstr "버섯을 기르기 위해 특별히 만들어진 선반입니다. 여기에 버섯 배양균을 심을 수 있습니다."

#: data\json\furniture_and_terrain\furniture-domestic_plants.json
msgid "freshly-planted mushroom rack"
msgstr "갓 심은 버섯 재배 선반"

#. ~ Description for freshly-planted mushroom rack
#: data\json\furniture_and_terrain\furniture-domestic_plants.json
msgid ""
"A rack specifically made for raising mushrooms.  This one contains a "
"mushroom culture that was recently planted."
msgstr "버섯을 기르기 위해 특별히 만들어진 선반입니다. 이것에는 최근에 심은 버섯 배양균이 있습니다."

#: data\json\furniture_and_terrain\furniture-domestic_plants.json
msgid "young mushroom rack"
msgstr "어린 버섯 재배 선반"

#. ~ Description for young mushroom rack
#: data\json\furniture_and_terrain\furniture-domestic_plants.json
msgid ""
"A rack specifically made for raising mushrooms.  This one contains a "
"mushroom culture that's just started to grow."
msgstr "버섯을 기르기 위해 특별히 만들어진 선반입니다. 이것에는 막 자라기 시작한 버섯 배양균이 있습니다."

#: data\json\furniture_and_terrain\furniture-domestic_plants.json
msgid "maturing mushroom rack"
msgstr "성장 중인 버섯 재배 선반"

#. ~ Description for maturing mushroom rack
#: data\json\furniture_and_terrain\furniture-domestic_plants.json
msgid ""
"A rack specifically made for raising mushrooms.  This one contains a growing"
" mushroom culture, that'll be ready to harvest soon."
msgstr "버섯을 기르기 위해 특별히 만들어진 선반입니다. 이것에는 곧 수확할 수 있을 만큼 자라는 버섯 배양균이 있습니다."

#: data\json\furniture_and_terrain\furniture-domestic_plants.json
msgid "harvestable mushroom rack"
msgstr "수확 가능한 버섯 재배 선반"

#. ~ Description for harvestable mushroom rack
#: data\json\furniture_and_terrain\furniture-domestic_plants.json
msgid ""
"A rack specifically made for raising mushrooms.  This one has mushrooms "
"ready to be picked growing in it."
msgstr "버섯을 기르기 위해 특별히 만들어진 선반입니다. 이것에는 딸 준비가 된 버섯이 자라고 있습니다."

#: data\json\furniture_and_terrain\furniture-eggs.json
msgid "spider egg sack"
msgstr "거미 알주머니"

#. ~ Description for spider egg sack
#: data\json\furniture_and_terrain\furniture-eggs.json
msgid ""
"Much too large, off-white egg sack.  Kind of icky.  Something IS moving in "
"there."
msgstr "지나치게 큰, 탁한 흰색의 알주머니입니다. 꽤 징그럽습니다. 안에서 무언가가 분명히 움직이고 있습니다."

#: data\json\furniture_and_terrain\furniture-eggs.json
#: data\json\furniture_and_terrain\furniture-migo.json
msgid "splat!"
msgstr "촤악!"

#. ~ Description for spider egg sack
#: data\json\furniture_and_terrain\furniture-eggs.json
msgid ""
"Bulbous mass of spider eggs.  More than kind of icky.  Something IS moving "
"in there."
msgstr "거미 알들이 부풀어 오른 덩어리입니다. 그냥 징그러운 정도가 아닙니다. 안에서 무언가가 분명히 움직이고 있습니다."

#. ~ Description for spider egg sack
#: data\json\furniture_and_terrain\furniture-eggs.json
msgid ""
"A horrifyingly oversized egg sack.  Something IS moving in there.  If you're"
" seeing this, you're already too close to it."
msgstr ""
"공포스러울 정도로 거대한 알주머니입니다. 안에서 무언가가 분명히 움직이고 있습니다. 이게 보인다면, 당신은 이미 너무 가까이 있는 "
"겁니다."

#: data\json\furniture_and_terrain\furniture-eggs.json
msgid "ruptured egg sack"
msgstr "터진 알주머니"

#. ~ Description for ruptured egg sack
#: data\json\furniture_and_terrain\furniture-eggs.json
msgid "Super icky.  Spider stuff's spilling out."
msgstr "엄청 징그럽습니다. 거미의 내용물이 쏟아져 나오고 있습니다."

#. ~ Description for swamp gas
#: data\json\furniture_and_terrain\furniture-emitters.json
msgid ""
"This is a pool of murky water, it occasionally bubbles, releasing a mildly "
"toxic gas."
msgstr "탁한 물이 고인 웅덩이로, 가끔 거품이 올라오며 약간 독성 있는 기체를 내뿜습니다."

#: data\json\furniture_and_terrain\furniture-emitters.json src/ballistics.cpp
#: src/map/map.cpp
msgid "splash!"
msgstr "철퍽!"

#. ~ Description for fog
#: data\json\furniture_and_terrain\furniture-emitters.json
msgid "This is a misty cloud of fog."
msgstr "안개 자욱한 구름입니다."

#: data\json\furniture_and_terrain\furniture-emitters.json
msgid "natural gas vent"
msgstr "천연가스 분출구"

#. ~ Description for natural gas vent
#: data\json\furniture_and_terrain\furniture-emitters.json
msgid "A natural gas vent on the lake bed that is currently emitting heat."
msgstr "현재 열을 내뿜고 있는 호수 바닥의 천연가스 분출구입니다."

#: data\json\furniture_and_terrain\furniture-emitters.json
msgid "running ventilation shutters"
msgstr "작동 중인 환기 셔터"

#. ~ Description for running ventilation shutters
#: data\json\furniture_and_terrain\furniture-emitters.json
msgid ""
"A large panel set into the reinforced metal wall.  Somehow still running "
"despite the chaos, blasting a wave of bitterly cold air into the facility."
msgstr ""
"보강된 금속 벽에 박힌 대형 패널입니다. 혼란 속에서도 어찌 아직 작동하며, 시리도록 차가운 공기를 시설 안으로 내뿜고 있습니다."

#: data\json\furniture_and_terrain\furniture-fakes.json
msgid "fake workbench hands"
msgstr "가짜 작업대 손"

#. ~ Description for fake workbench hands
#: data\json\furniture_and_terrain\furniture-fakes.json
msgid "This fake workbench holds the stats for working on a wielded item."
msgstr "이 가짜 작업대는 손에 쥔 아이템 작업 시 스탯을 담고 있습니다."

#: data\json\furniture_and_terrain\furniture-fakes.json
msgid "ground crafting spot"
msgstr "지면 제작 지점"

#. ~ Description for ground crafting spot
#: data\json\furniture_and_terrain\furniture-fakes.json
msgid ""
"A cleared spot on the ground for crafting.  Slower than using a workbench or"
" holding a project in your hands, but readily available."
msgstr "제작을 위해 정리된 지면 공간입니다. 작업대를 쓰거나 손에 들고 작업하는 것보다 느리지만, 바로 쓸 수 있습니다."

#. ~ Description for seeing this is a bug
#: data\json\furniture_and_terrain\furniture-fakes.json
msgid "Seeing this is a bug.  If seen, please report and destroy."
msgstr "이게 보인다면 버그입니다. 보이면 신고하고 제거해주세요."

#: data\json\furniture_and_terrain\furniture-fireplaces.json
msgid "fireplace"
msgstr "벽난로"

#. ~ Description for fireplace
#: data\json\furniture_and_terrain\furniture-fireplaces.json
msgid ""
"Ah.  The relaxation of sitting in front of a fire as the world around you "
"crumbles.  Towards the End, you could also get this service on your "
"television."
msgstr "아. 주변 세계가 무너져가는 와중에 모닥불 앞에 앉는 여유. 종말 직전에는 텔레비전으로도 이 서비스를 받을 수 있었습니다."

#: data\json\furniture_and_terrain\furniture-fireplaces.json
#: data\json\furniture_and_terrain\furniture-graves.json
#: data\json\furniture_and_terrain\furniture-industrial.json
#: data\json\furniture_and_terrain\furniture-seats.json
#: data\json\furniture_and_terrain\furniture-terrains.json
#: data\json\furniture_and_terrain\furniture-tools.json
#: data\json\furniture_and_terrain\terrain-doors.json
#: data\json\furniture_and_terrain\terrain-fences-gates.json
#: data\json\furniture_and_terrain\terrain-floors-outdoors.json
#: data\json\furniture_and_terrain\terrain-manufactured.json
#: data\json\furniture_and_terrain\terrain-mechanisms.json
#: data\json\furniture_and_terrain\terrain-railroads.json
#: data\json\furniture_and_terrain\terrain-roofs.json
#: data\json\furniture_and_terrain\terrain-triffid.json
