#: data\json\items\comestibles\nuts.json
msgid "Delicious hickory nut ambrosia.  A drink worthy of the gods."
msgstr "신들의 음료라는 말에 걸맞은 맛있는 히코리 열매 암브로시아입니다."

#: data\json\items\comestibles\nuts.json
msgid "acorns"
msgid_plural "acorns"
msgstr[0] "도토리"

#. ~ Description for {'str_sp': 'acorns'}
#: data\json\items\comestibles\nuts.json
msgid ""
"A handful of acorns, still in their shells.  Squirrels like them, but "
"they're not very good for you to eat in this state."
msgstr "껍질을 까지 않은 도토리 한 줌. 다람쥐가 좋아하는 음식. 이 상태로 먹긴 힘들다."

#: data\json\items\comestibles\nuts.json
msgid "roasted acorns"
msgid_plural "roasted acorns"
msgstr[0] "볶은 도토리"

#. ~ Description for {'str_sp': 'roasted acorns'}
#: data\json\items\comestibles\nuts.json
msgid "A handful roasted nuts from an oak tree."
msgstr "떡갈나무에서 난 열매를 볶은 것입니다."

#: data\json\items\comestibles\nuts.json
msgid "cooked acorn meal"
msgid_plural "cooked acorn meal"
msgstr[0] "도토리 (요리됨)"

#. ~ Description for {'str_sp': 'cooked acorn meal'}
#: data\json\items\comestibles\nuts.json
msgid ""
"A serving of acorns that have been hulled, chopped, and boiled in water "
"before being thoroughly toasted until dry.  Filling and nutritious."
msgstr "껍질을 까고 다지고 물에 끓인 후 마르기 전까지 구운 도토리 요리. 속을 채워주고 건강에 좋다."

#: data\json\items\comestibles\offal_dishes.json
msgid "foie gras"
msgid_plural "foie gras"
msgstr[0] "푸아그라"

#. ~ Description for {'str_sp': 'foie gras'}
#: data\json\items\comestibles\offal_dishes.json
msgid ""
"Though it's not technically foie gras, you don't have to think about that."
msgstr "기술적으로 푸아그라는 아니지만, 그건 신경 쓰지 않아도 됩니다."

#: data\json\items\comestibles\offal_dishes.json
msgid "liver & onions"
msgid_plural "liver & onions"
msgstr[0] "간과 양파"

#. ~ Description for {'str_sp': 'liver & onions'}
#: data\json\items\comestibles\offal_dishes.json
msgid "A classic way to serve liver."
msgstr "간을 제공하는 고전적인 방법."

#: data\json\items\comestibles\offal_dishes.json
msgid "fried liver"
msgid_plural "fried livers"
msgstr[0] "간 튀김"

#. ~ Description for fried liver
#. ~ Description for deep-fried tripe
#: data\json\items\comestibles\offal_dishes.json
msgid "Nothing tastier than something that's deep-fried!"
msgstr "세상에서 튀김보다 더 맛있는 것은 없다."

#: data\json\items\comestibles\offal_dishes.json
msgid "humble pie"
msgid_plural "humble pies"
msgstr[0] "험블 파이"

#. ~ Description for humble pie
#: data\json\items\comestibles\offal_dishes.json
msgid ""
"Also known as 'Umble' pie, made with chopped organ meats.  Not half bad, and"
" really good for you!"
msgstr "'엄블' 파이로도 알려진, 다진 내장으로 만든 파이입니다. 나쁘지 않고, 몸에도 아주 좋습니다!"

#: data\json\items\comestibles\offal_dishes.json
msgid "stewed tripe"
msgid_plural "stewed tripes"
msgstr[0] "양깃머리 조림"

#. ~ Description for stewed tripe
#: data\json\items\comestibles\offal_dishes.json
msgid ""
"Stomach lining, cut up and stewed for an hour in broth.  Better than it "
"sounds."
msgstr "위벽을 잘라 육수에 한 시간 조렸습니다. 듣는 것보다 낫습니다."

#: data\json\items\comestibles\offal_dishes.json
msgid "deep-fried tripe"
msgid_plural "deep-fried tripes"
msgstr[0] "양깃머리 튀김"

#: data\json\items\comestibles\offal_dishes.json
msgid "leverpostej"
msgid_plural "leverpostej"
msgstr[0] "레버포스테이"

#. ~ Description for {'str_sp': 'leverpostej'}
#: data\json\items\comestibles\offal_dishes.json
msgid ""
"A traditional Danish pate.  Probably better if you spread it on some bread."
msgstr "전통 덴마크식 파테입니다. 빵에 발라 먹으면 더 맛있을 것입니다."

#: data\json\items\comestibles\offal_dishes.json
msgid "cooked brains"
msgid_plural "cooked brains"
msgstr[0] "요리된 뇌"

#. ~ Description for {'str_sp': 'cooked brains'}
#: data\json\items\comestibles\offal_dishes.json
msgid ""
"Now you can emulate those zombies you love so much!  Preparing brain for "
"eating is challenging, and this doesn't seem to be the best way to do it."
msgstr ""
"이제 당신이 그토록 사랑하는 좀비들을 따라할 수 있습니다! 뇌를 먹기 위한 조리는 어렵고, 이것이 최선의 방법은 아닌 것 같습니다."

#: data\json\items\comestibles\offal_dishes.json
msgid "fried brain"
msgid_plural "fried brains"
msgstr[0] "뇌 튀김"

#. ~ Description for fried brain
#: data\json\items\comestibles\offal_dishes.json
msgid "I don't know what you were expecting.  It's deep-fried."
msgstr "뭘 기대했는지 모르겠습니다. 튀긴 겁니다."

#: data\json\items\comestibles\offal_dishes.json
msgid "cooked kidney"
msgid_plural "cooked kidneys"
msgstr[0] "요리된 콩팥"

#. ~ Description for cooked kidney
#: data\json\items\comestibles\offal_dishes.json
msgid "No, this is not beans."
msgstr "콩이랑 헷갈리지 말 것."

#: data\json\items\comestibles\offal_dishes.json
msgid "deviled kidney"
msgid_plural "deviled kidneys"
msgstr[0] "데빌드 키드니"

#. ~ Description for deviled kidney
#: data\json\items\comestibles\offal_dishes.json
msgid "A delicious way to prepare kidneys."
msgstr "콩팥을 맛있게 조리하는 방법."

#: data\json\items\comestibles\offal_dishes.json
msgid "cooked sweetbread"
msgid_plural "cooked sweetbreads"
msgstr[0] "스위트브레드 (요리됨)"

#. ~ Description for cooked sweetbread
#: data\json\items\comestibles\offal_dishes.json
msgid "Normally a delicacy, it needs a little… something."
msgstr "보통은 별미지만, 약간… 뭔가가 필요합니다."

#: data\json\items\comestibles\offal_dishes.json
msgid "grilled sweetbread"
msgid_plural "grilled sweetbreads"
msgstr[0] "구운 스위트브레드"

#. ~ Description for grilled sweetbread
#: data\json\items\comestibles\offal_dishes.json
msgid "Not sweet, like the name would suggest, but delicious all the same!"
msgstr "이름과 달리 달지는 않지만, 그래도 맛있습니다!"

#: data\json\items\comestibles\offal_dishes.json
msgid "cooked liver"
msgid_plural "cooked livers"
msgstr[0] "요리된 간"

#. ~ Description for cooked liver
#: data\json\items\comestibles\offal_dishes.json
msgid ""
"Chock-full of B-Vitamins!  Cooked liver isn't all that bad, depending on how"
" you feel about the texture, but this is probably the least fancy way to do "
"it."
msgstr ""
"B비타민 가득! 조리된 간도 질감을 어떻게 생각하느냐에 따라 그리 나쁘진 않지만, 이건 아마 가장 근사하지 않은 조리법일 것입니다."

#: data\json\items\comestibles\offal_dishes.json
msgid "canned liver"
msgid_plural "canned livers"
msgstr[0] "간 통조림"

#. ~ Description for canned liver
#: data\json\items\comestibles\offal_dishes.json
msgid "Livers preserved in a can.  Chock-full of B vitamins!"
msgstr "통조림에 보존된 간입니다. B비타민 가득!"

#: data\json\items\comestibles\offal_dishes.json
msgid "cooked piece of lung"
msgid_plural "cooked pieces of lung"
msgstr[0] "폐 조각(요리됨)"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'cooked piece of lung', 'str_pl': 'cooked pieces
#. of lung'}
#: data\json\items\comestibles\offal_dishes.json
msgid ""
" Prepared in this way, it's a chewy grayish lump of flavorless connective "
"tissue.  It doesn't look any tastier than it did raw, but the parasites are "
"all cooked out."
msgstr " 이렇게 조리하면, 맛없는 연회색 결합조직 덩어리가 됩니다. 날것일 때보다 맛있어 보이진 않지만, 기생충은 다 죽었습니다."

#: data\json\items\comestibles\offal_dishes.json
msgid "lung provence"
msgid_plural "lung provences"
msgstr[0] "프로방스식 폐 요리"

#. ~ Description for lung provence
#: data\json\items\comestibles\offal_dishes.json
msgid "A delicious way to prepare lungs."
msgstr "폐를 맛있게 준비하는 방법입니다."

#: data\json\items\comestibles\offal_dishes.json
msgid "toettchen"
msgid_plural "toettchens"
msgstr[0] "퇴트헨"

#. ~ Description for toettchen
#. ~ Description for tÖttchen
#: data\json\items\comestibles\offal_dishes.json
#: data\json\obsoletion\items.json
msgid "A German lung dish."
msgstr "독일식 폐 요리입니다."

#: data\json\items\comestibles\offal_dishes.json
msgid "scrambled eggs and brain"
msgid_plural "scrambled eggs and brains"
msgstr[0] "뇌 스크램블 에그"

#. ~ Description for scrambled eggs and brain
#: data\json\items\comestibles\offal_dishes.json
msgid "Brains and eggs, why didn't you ever think to put these together?"
msgstr "뇌와 계란, 왜 이 둘을 같이 할 생각을 못 했을까요?"

#: data\json\items\comestibles\offal_dishes.json
msgid "sausage casing"
msgid_plural "sausage casings"
msgstr[0] "소시지 케이싱"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'sausage casing'}
#: data\json\items\comestibles\offal_dishes.json
msgid ""
"Sausage casings made from animal intestines.  Ready to be used for forming "
"meat products."
msgstr "동물 내장으로 만든 소시지 케이싱입니다. 육제품 성형에 바로 쓸 수 있습니다."

#: data\json\items\comestibles\offal_dishes.json
msgid "artificial sausage casing"
msgid_plural "artificial sausage casings"
msgstr[0] "인조 소시지 케이싱"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'artificial sausage casing'}
#: data\json\items\comestibles\offal_dishes.json
msgid ""
"Sausage casings made from plastic.  Ready to be used for forming meat "
"products."
msgstr "플라스틱으로 만든 소시지 케이싱입니다. 육제품 성형에 바로 쓸 수 있습니다."

#: data\json\items\comestibles\offal_dishes.json
msgid "homemade hot dog"
msgid_plural "homemade hot dogs"
msgstr[0] "수제 핫도그"

#: data\json\items\comestibles\offal_dishes.json
msgid "fried offal"
msgid_plural "fried offal"
msgstr[0] "내장 튀김"

#. ~ Conditional name for {'str_sp': 'fried offal'} when VITAMIN matches
#. human_flesh_vitamin
#: data\json\items\comestibles\offal_dishes.json
msgid "fried Frank offal"
msgid_plural "fried Frank offals"
msgstr[0] "프랭크 내장 튀김"

#. ~ Conditional name for {'str_sp': 'fried offal'} when COMPONENT_ID matches
#. mutant
#: data\json\items\comestibles\offal_dishes.json
msgid "fried freak offal"
msgid_plural "fried freak offal"
msgstr[0] "괴물 내장 튀김"

#. ~ Description for {'str_sp': 'fried offal'}
#: data\json\items\comestibles\offal_dishes.json
msgid ""
"This is freshly cooked organ meat and entrails.  Deep-frying it makes it "
"more palatable, and while it's probably less healthy it's still filled with "
"essential vitamins."
msgstr "갓 조리된 장기 고기와 내장입니다. 튀기면 먹을 만해지고, 건강엔 덜 좋을 수 있지만 여전히 필수 비타민으로 가득합니다."

#: data\json\items\comestibles\other.json
msgid "diet pill"
msgid_plural "diet pills"
msgstr[0] "다이어트 약"

#. ~ Description for diet pill
#: data\json\items\comestibles\other.json
msgid ""
"Not very nutritious.  Warning: contains calories, unsuitable for "
"breatharians."
msgstr "별로 영양가는 없습니다. 경고: 칼로리 있음, 동력 호흡기 사용에 부적절함."

#: data\json\items\comestibles\other.json
msgid "blob glob"
msgid_plural "blob globs"
msgstr[0] "블럽 조각"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'blob glob'}
#: data\json\items\comestibles\other.json
msgid ""
"A little hunk of glop that fell off a blob monster.  It doesn't seem "
"hostile, but it does wiggle occasionally."
msgstr "블럽 괴물에서 떨어진 작은 덩어리 조각입니다. 적대적이지는 않은 것 같지만, 가끔 꿈틀거립니다."

#: data\json\items\comestibles\other.json
msgid "honey comb"
msgid_plural "honey combs"
msgstr[0] "벌집"

#. ~ Description for honey comb
#: data\json\items\comestibles\other.json
msgid "A large chunk of wax filled with honey.  Very tasty."
msgstr "꿀로 채워진 큰 밀랍 덩어리입니다. 아주 맛있습니다."

#: data\json\items\comestibles\other.json
msgid "wax"
msgid_plural "waxes"
msgstr[0] "밀랍"

#. ~ Description for {'str_pl': 'waxes', 'str': 'wax'}
#: data\json\items\comestibles\other.json
msgid ""
"A large chunk of beeswax.  Not very tasty or nourishing, but okay in an "
"emergency."
msgstr "큰 밀랍 덩어리입니다. 그다지 맛있지도 않고, 영양소도 풍부하지 않지만, 배가 고프다면 이런 음식이라도 괜찮을 것 같습니다."

#: data\json\items\comestibles\other.json
#: data\mods\ProjectSquirrel\items\advtech\sq_meds.json
msgid "royal jelly"
msgid_plural "royal jellies"
msgstr[0] "로얄 젤리"

#. ~ Use action activation_message for {'str': 'royal jelly', 'str_pl': 'royal
#. jellies'}.
#: data\json\items\comestibles\other.json
#: data\mods\ProjectSquirrel\items\advtech\sq_meds.json
msgid "You feel warm inside after eating the royal jelly."
msgstr "로열젤리를 먹으니 속이 따뜻해진다."

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'royal jelly', 'str_pl': 'royal jellies'}
#: data\json\items\comestibles\other.json
msgid ""
"A translucent hexagonal chunk of wax, filled with dense, milky jelly.  Rich "
"with the most beneficial substances post-cataclysm hives can produce, it can"
" cure various afflictions and serve as an antitoxin.  However, it's also "
"rich in mutagenic toxins of its own, given the creatures producing it."
msgstr ""
"걸쭉하고 우유빛 젤리로 채워진 반투명 육각 밀랍 덩어리입니다. 대재앙 이후 벌집이 생산할 수 있는 가장 유익한 물질이 풍부해 다양한 "
"고통을 치료하고 해독제 역할을 할 수 있습니다. 하지만 이걸 만드는 생물을 고려하면, 자체 돌연변이 독소도 풍부합니다."

#: data\json\items\comestibles\other.json
#: data\json\items\comestibles\seed.json data\mods\No_Fungi\comestibles.json
msgid "marloss berry"
msgid_plural "marloss berries"
msgstr[0] "말로스 열매"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'marloss berry', 'str_pl': 'marloss berries'}
#: data\json\items\comestibles\other.json
msgid ""
"This looks like a blueberry the size of your fist, but pinkish in color.  It"
" has a strong but delicious aroma, but is clearly either mutated or of alien"
" origin."
msgstr ""
"블루베리와 비슷해보이며, 크기는 주먹 정도입니다만, 색은 분홍빛이 돕니다. 맛있는 향기가 강하게 나지만, 이 열매는 분명히 변이된 "
"것이거나 외계에서 왔을 겁니다."

#: data\json\items\comestibles\other.json data\mods\No_Fungi\comestibles.json
msgid "marloss gelatin"
msgid_plural "marloss gelatin"
msgstr[0] "말로스 젤라틴"

#. ~ Description for {'str_sp': 'marloss gelatin'}
#: data\json\items\comestibles\other.json
msgid ""
"This looks like a handful of lemon-colored liquid which has taken a set, "
"much like pre-Cataclysm Jello.  It has a strong but delicious aroma, but is "
"clearly either mutated or of alien origin."
msgstr ""
"대재앙 이전 젤로처럼 굳은, 레몬색 액체 한 줌처럼 보입니다. 강렬하면서 맛있는 향이 나지만, 분명히 돌연변이거나 외계 기원입니다."

#: data\json\items\comestibles\other.json
#: data\json\items\comestibles\seed.json data\mods\No_Fungi\comestibles.json
msgid "mycus fruit"
msgid_plural "mycus fruits"
msgstr[0] "미커스 열매"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'mycus fruit'}
#: data\json\items\comestibles\other.json
msgid ""
"Humans might call this a Gray Delicious apple: large, gray, and smells even "
"better than the Marloss.  If they didn't reject it for its alien origins.  "
"But we know better."
msgstr ""
"인간은 이것을 회색의 맛있는 사과라고 부르겠죠:크고, 회색이고, 말로스보다도 좋은 향기가 나니까 말입니다. 외계물질이라며 이걸 거부하지 "
"않았다면 말입니다만, 우리는 그렇지 않습니다."

#: data\json\items\comestibles\other.json
msgid "yeast"
msgid_plural "yeast"
msgstr[0] "이스트"

#. ~ Description for {'str_sp': 'yeast'}
#: data\json\items\comestibles\other.json
msgid ""
"A powder-like mix of cultured yeast, good for baking and brewing alike."
msgstr "가루 형태로 배양된 효모입니다. 제빵이나 양조에 쓰입니다."

#: data\json\items\comestibles\other.json
msgid "bone meal"
msgid_plural "bone meal"
msgstr[0] "뼛가루"

#. ~ Description for {'str_sp': 'bone meal'}
#: data\json\items\comestibles\other.json
msgid "This bone meal can be used to craft fertilizer and some other things."
msgstr "이 뼛가루는 비료와 다른 것들을 만드는 데 사용될 수 있다."

#: data\json\items\comestibles\other.json
msgid "tainted bone meal"
msgid_plural "tainted bone meal"
msgstr[0] "오염된 뼛가루"

#. ~ Description for {'str_sp': 'tainted bone meal'}
#: data\json\items\comestibles\other.json
msgid "This is a grayish bone meal made from rotten bones."
msgstr "오염된 뼈를 갈아 만든 회색 뼛가루."

#: data\json\items\comestibles\other.json
msgid "chitin powder"
msgid_plural "chitin powder"
msgstr[0] "키틴질 가루"

#. ~ Description for {'str_sp': 'chitin powder'}
#: data\json\items\comestibles\other.json
msgid ""
"This chitin powder can be used to craft fertilizer and some other things."
msgstr "이 키틴질 가루는 비료와 다른 것들을 만드는 데 사용될 수 있다."

#: data\json\items\comestibles\other.json
msgid "cardboard"
msgid_plural "cardboards"
msgstr[0] "골판지"

#. ~ Description for cardboard
#: data\json\items\comestibles\other.json
msgid "A piece of cardboard."
msgstr "골판지 한 조각입니다."

#: data\json\items\comestibles\other.json
msgid "canned beans"
msgid_plural "beans"
msgstr[0] "콩 통조림"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'canned beans', 'str_pl': 'beans'}
#: data\json\items\comestibles\other.json
msgid ""
"Canned beans.  A staple among canned goods, these are reputedly good for "
"one's coronary health."
msgstr "통조림 콩입니다. 통조림 식품 중에서도 콩은 보통 건강에 좋은 것으로 알려졌습니다."

#: data\json\items\comestibles\other.json
msgid "dried beans"
msgid_plural "dried beans"
msgstr[0] "말린 콩"

#. ~ Description for {'str_sp': 'dried beans'}
#: data\json\items\comestibles\other.json
msgid ""
"Dehydrated great northern beans.  Tasty and nutritious when cooked, "
"virtually inedible when dry."
msgstr "마른 흰콩. 조리하면 배부르고 맛있게 먹을 수 있지만, 건조된 상태로는 먹기 힘들다."

#: data\json\items\comestibles\other.json
msgid "cooked beans"
msgid_plural "cooked beans"
msgstr[0] "콩 (요리됨)"

#. ~ Description for {'str_sp': 'cooked beans'}
#: data\json\items\comestibles\other.json
msgid "A hearty serving of cooked great northern beans."
msgstr "따뜻하게 조리된 북부 대형 콩."

#: data\json\items\comestibles\other.json
msgid "tofu"
msgid_plural "tofu"
msgstr[0] "두부"

#. ~ Description for {'str_sp': 'tofu'}
#. ~ Description for {'str_sp': 'fried tofu'}
#: data\json\items\comestibles\other.json
msgid ""
"Tofu, a soy protein crucial to East Asian cuisine.  It absorbs flavors very "
"well and can be used as a meat alternative in many dishes."
msgstr "동아시아 요리에 필수적인 콩 단백질, 두부입니다. 풍미를 아주 잘 흡수하고 많은 요리에서 고기 대체재로 쓸 수 있습니다."

#: data\json\items\comestibles\other.json
msgid "fried tofu"
msgid_plural "fried tofu"
msgstr[0] "두부 튀김"

#: data\json\items\comestibles\other.json
msgid "dehydrated tofu"
msgid_plural "dehydrated tofu"
msgstr[0] "건조 두부"

#. ~ Description for {'str_sp': 'dehydrated tofu'}
#: data\json\items\comestibles\other.json
msgid "Dehydrated tofu, sealed and still extra firm to last a long time."
msgstr "오래가도록 밀봉되어 여전히 매우 단단한 건조 두부입니다."

#: data\json\items\comestibles\other.json
msgid "soybeans"
msgid_plural "soybeans"
msgstr[0] "콩"

#. ~ Description for {'str_sp': 'soybeans'}
#: data\json\items\comestibles\other.json
msgid ""
"Light brown beans, they have many uses, mildly toxic and not recommended, "
"but you could eat them raw."
msgstr "연갈색 콩으로, 쓰임이 많고 약간 독성이 있어 권장되진 않지만 날로 먹을 수도 있습니다."

#: data\json\items\comestibles\other.json
msgid "raw edamame"
msgid_plural "raw edamames"
msgstr[0] "날 에다마메"

#. ~ Description for raw edamame
#: data\json\items\comestibles\other.json
msgid ""
"Light green raw edamame still in its pod, you should boil or freeze these, "
"or you could eat them while they are still toxic."
msgstr "아직 꼬투리에 든 연녹색 날 에다마메로, 삶거나 얼려야 합니다. 아니면 아직 독성이 있는 채로 먹을 수도 있습니다."

#: data\json\items\comestibles\other.json
msgid "dried lentils"
msgid_plural "dried lentils"
msgstr[0] "마른 렌틸콩"

#. ~ Description for {'str_sp': 'dried lentils'}
#: data\json\items\comestibles\other.json
msgid ""
"A humble but nutrient-rich legume.  Should be cooked prior to consumption."
msgstr "소박하지만 영양이 풍부한 콩입니다. 먹기 전에 조리해야 합니다."

#: data\json\items\comestibles\other.json
msgid "Foodplace's delicious food™"
msgid_plural "Foodplace's delicious food™"
msgstr[0] "푸드플레이스의 맛있는 음식™"

#. ~ Description for {'str_sp': "Foodplace's delicious food™"}
#: data\json\items\comestibles\other.json
msgid ""
"The best-seller from Foodplace, delicious food™, is made with real foodstuff"
" and is guaranteed 100% edible!"
msgstr "진짜 식품 재료로 만들어 100% 먹을 수 있음이 보장되는, 푸드플레이스의 베스트셀러 맛있는 음식™입니다!"

#: data\json\items\comestibles\other.json
msgid "cooked lentils"
msgid_plural "cooked lentils"
msgstr[0] "조리된 렌틸콩"

#. ~ Description for {'str_sp': 'cooked lentils'}
#: data\json\items\comestibles\other.json
msgid "Some delicious cooked lentils.  Humble but nutrient-rich."
msgstr "맛있는 조리된 렌틸콩입니다. 소박하지만 영양이 풍부합니다."

#: data\json\items\comestibles\other.json
msgid "coffee powder"
msgid_plural "coffee powder"
msgstr[0] "커피 가루"

#. ~ Description for {'str_sp': 'coffee powder'}
#: data\json\items\comestibles\other.json
msgid ""
"Ground coffee beans.  You can boil it into a mediocre stimulant, or "
"something better if you had an atomic coffee pot."
msgstr "갈아 놓은 커피콩. 끓여서 보통 수준의 각성제로 마시거나, 원자력 커피 포트가 있다면 더 좋은 것을 만들 수 있습니다."

#: data\json\items\comestibles\other.json
msgid "Kentucky coffee grounds"
msgid_plural "Kentucky coffee grounds"
msgstr[0] "켄터키 커피 가루"

#. ~ Description for {'str_sp': 'Kentucky coffee grounds'}
#: data\json\items\comestibles\other.json
msgid ""
"Coffee grounds created through washing, cleaning, and roasting the pods from"
" a Kentucky coffeetree.  They can be used to create coffee."
msgstr "켄터키 커피나무의 열매를 씻고, 세척하고, 볶아 만든 커피 가루입니다. 커피를 만드는 데 쓸 수 있습니다."

#: data\json\items\comestibles\other.json
msgid "candied honey"
msgid_plural "candied honey"
msgstr[0] "굳은 꿀"

#. ~ Description for {'str_sp': 'candied honey'}
#: data\json\items\comestibles\other.json
msgid ""
"Honey, that stuff the bees make.  This variant is \"candied honey\", a "
"variant of very thick consistence.  This honey won't spoil and is good for "
"your digestion."
msgstr "액상의 벌이 만든 벌꿀로 아주 뻑뻑하게 굳은 \"굳은 꿀\"이다. 이 꿀은 절대 상하지 않고 소화하기 좋다."

#: data\json\items\comestibles\other.json
msgid "canned tomato"
msgid_plural "canned tomatoes"
msgstr[0] "토마토 통조림"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'canned tomato', 'str_pl': 'canned tomatoes'}
#: data\json\items\comestibles\other.json
msgid ""
"Canned tomato.  A staple in many pantries, and useful for many recipes."
msgstr "토마토 통조림. 일반적인 식료품 저장고의 주 구성품으로, 여러 조리법에 유용하게 사용된다."

#: data\json\items\comestibles\other.json
msgid "embalmed human brain"
msgid_plural "embalmed human brains"
msgstr[0] "방부 처리된 인간 두뇌"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'embalmed human brain'}
#: data\json\items\comestibles\other.json
msgid ""
"This is a human brain soaked in a solution of highly toxic formaldehyde.  "
"Eating this would be a terrible idea."
msgstr "독성이 매우 강한 포름알데히드 용액에 담긴 인간의 뇌입니다. 이것을 먹는 것은 끔찍한 생각입니다."

#: data\json\items\comestibles\other.json
#: data\mods\DinoMod\items\petfoods.json
msgid "cattle fodder"
msgid_plural "cattle fodder"
msgstr[0] "소 사료"

#. ~ Description for {'str_sp': 'cattle fodder'}
#: data\json\items\comestibles\other.json
msgid ""
"What cattle eat.  Mainly made of grass, silage or legumes.  It's perfect for"
" ruminants.  Activate it to attempt to tame an adjacent wild animal, or to "
"feed it to pets to speed up healing and productivity."
msgstr ""
"가축이 먹는 것입니다. 주로 풀, 사일리지, 콩으로 만듭니다. 반추동물에게 완벽합니다. 사용하면 인접한 야생동물 길들이기를 시도하거나, "
"반려동물에게 먹여 회복과 생산성을 높입니다."

#: data\json\items\comestibles\other.json
msgid "bird food"
msgid_plural "bird food"
msgstr[0] "새 모이"

#. ~ Description for {'str_sp': 'bird food'}
#: data\json\items\comestibles\other.json
msgid ""
"What birds eat.  Mainly made of seeds, silage or legumes.  It's perfect for "
"small birds.  Activate it to attempt to tame an adjacent wild animal, or to "
"feed it to pets to speed up healing and productivity."
msgstr ""
"새가 먹는 것입니다. 주로 씨앗, 사일리지, 콩으로 만듭니다. 작은 새에게 완벽합니다. 사용하면 인접한 야생동물 길들이기를 시도하거나, "
"반려동물에게 먹여 회복과 생산성을 높입니다."

#: data\json\items\comestibles\other.json
msgid "dog food"
msgid_plural "dog food"
msgstr[0] "개 사료"

#. ~ Description for {'str_sp': 'dog food'}
#: data\json\items\comestibles\other.json
msgid ""
"This is food for dogs.  It smells strange, but dogs seem to love it.  "
"Activate it to attempt to tame an adjacent wild animal, or to feed it to "
"pets to speed up healing and productivity."
msgstr ""
"개 사료입니다. 냄새가 이상하지만 개들은 좋아하는 것 같습니다. 사용하면 인접한 야생동물 길들이기를 시도하거나, 반려동물에게 먹여 회복과"
" 생산성을 높입니다."

#: data\json\items\comestibles\other.json
msgid "cat food"
msgid_plural "cat food"
msgstr[0] "고양이 사료"

#. ~ Description for {'str_sp': 'cat food'}
#: data\json\items\comestibles\other.json
msgid ""
"This is food for cats.  It smells strange, but cats seem to love it.  "
"Activate it to attempt to tame an adjacent wild animal, or to feed it to "
"pets to speed up healing and productivity."
msgstr ""
"고양이 사료입니다. 냄새가 이상하지만 고양이들은 좋아하는 것 같습니다. 사용하면 인접한 야생동물 길들이기를 시도하거나, 반려동물에게 먹여"
" 회복과 생산성을 높입니다."

#: data\json\items\comestibles\other.json
msgid "jellied insects"
msgid_plural "jellied insects"
msgstr[0] "곤충 젤리"

#. ~ Description for {'str_sp': 'jellied insects'}
#: data\json\items\comestibles\other.json
msgid ""
"Preserved insect organs, perfect for animals who like extra proteins.  "
"Activate it to attempt to tame an adjacent wild animal, or to feed it to "
"pets to speed up healing and productivity."
msgstr ""
"보존된 곤충 장기로, 단백질을 추가로 좋아하는 동물에게 완벽합니다. 사용하면 인접한 야생동물 길들이기를 시도하거나, 반려동물에게 먹여 "
"회복과 생산성을 높입니다."

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'grass', 'str_pl': 'grasses'}
#: data\json\items\comestibles\other.json
msgid ""
"Some grass, edible by grazers and ruminants only.  Seeing this item is a "
"bug."
msgstr "풀입니다. 방목동물과 반추동물만 먹을 수 있습니다. 이 아이템이 보인다면 버그입니다."

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'underbrush', 'str_pl': 'underbrushes'}
#: data\json\items\comestibles\other.json
msgid "Some underbrush, edible by ruminants only.  Seeing this item is a bug."
msgstr "덤불입니다. 반추동물만 먹을 수 있습니다. 이 아이템이 보인다면 버그입니다."

#: data\json\items\comestibles\other.json
msgid "nectar"
msgid_plural "nectars"
msgstr[0] "꿀즙"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'nectar'}
#: data\json\items\comestibles\other.json
msgid "Some nectar.  Seeing this item is a bug."
msgstr "꿀즙입니다. 이 아이템이 보인다면 버그입니다."

#: data\json\items\comestibles\protein.json
msgid "protein drink"
msgid_plural "protein drinks"
msgstr[0] "단백질 음료"

#. ~ Conditional name for protein drink when VITAMIN matches
#. human_flesh_vitamin
#: data\json\items\comestibles\protein.json
msgid "soylent green drink"
msgid_plural "soylent green drinks"
msgstr[0] "소일렌트 그린 음료"

#. ~ Conditional name for protein drink when COMPONENT_ID matches mutant
#. ~ Conditional name for {'str_sp': 'protein powder'} when COMPONENT_ID
#. matches mutant
#. ~ Conditional name for protein shake when COMPONENT_ID matches mutant
#. ~ Conditional name for fortified protein shake when COMPONENT_ID matches
#. mutant
#: data\json\items\comestibles\protein.json
#, c-format
msgid "perturbing %s"
msgid_plural "perturbing %s"
msgstr[0] "불안한 %s"

#. ~ Description for protein drink
#: data\json\items\comestibles\protein.json
msgid ""
"A thin slurry of refined protein mixed with water.  While quite nutritious, "
"it is not particularly tasty."
msgstr "정제된 단백질과 물을 섞어 만든, 약간 걸쭉한 액체입니다. 꽤 영양소가 높지만, 아직 별로 맛은 없습니다."

#: data\json\items\comestibles\protein.json
msgid "protein powder"
msgid_plural "protein powder"
msgstr[0] "단백질 가루"

#. ~ Conditional name for {'str_sp': 'protein powder'} when VITAMIN matches
#. human_flesh_vitamin
#: data\json\items\comestibles\protein.json
msgid "soylent green powder"
msgid_plural "soylent green powder"
msgstr[0] "소일렌트 그린 분말"

#. ~ Description for {'str_sp': 'protein powder'}
#: data\json\items\comestibles\protein.json
msgid ""
"Raw, refined protein.  While quite nutritious, it is impossible to enjoy in "
"its pure form, try adding water."
msgstr "생 정제 단백질. 꽤 영양가 있지만, 순수한 형태로는 즐기기 불가능합니다. 물을 넣어 보세요."

#: data\json\items\comestibles\protein.json
msgid "protein ration"
msgid_plural "protein rations"
msgstr[0] "단백질 배급식"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'protein ration'}
#: data\json\items\comestibles\protein.json
msgid ""
"SoyPelusa ran a highly successful crowdfunding campaign for this protein "
"bar.  A person can live on one of these bars, three times a day, presumably "
"forever.  After backers received their product, a single flaw was found: "
"most consumers found starvation preferable to the flavor.  Warehouses of the"
" product went unsold as the company went bankrupt, providing the perfect "
"opportunity for FEMA to scoop them up and stock the evac shelters.  Now, you"
" hold a piece of famous crowdfunding history in your hands.  How exciting."
msgstr ""
"소이펠루사가 이 단백질 바로 크게 성공한 크라우드펀딩을 진행했습니다. 사람이 이 바 하나를 하루 세 번 먹고, 아마 영원히, 살 수 "
"있습니다. 후원자들이 제품을 받은 후 단 하나의 결함이 발견됐습니다: 대부분의 소비자가 맛보다 굶주림을 선택했습니다. 회사가 파산하면서 "
"창고의 제품이 팔리지 않았고, FEMA가 쓸어가 피난 대피소에 비치할 완벽한 기회가 됐습니다. 이제, 당신은 유명한 크라우드펀딩 역사의 "
"한 조각을 손에 들고 있습니다. 얼마나 신나나요."

#: data\json\items\comestibles\protein.json
msgid "protein shake"
msgid_plural "protein shakes"
msgstr[0] "단백질 셰이크"

#. ~ Conditional name for protein shake when VITAMIN matches
#. human_flesh_vitamin
#: data\json\items\comestibles\protein.json
msgid "soylent green shake"
msgid_plural "soylent green shakes"
msgstr[0] "소일렌트 그린 셰이크"

#. ~ Description for protein shake
#: data\json\items\comestibles\protein.json
msgid ""
"A thick and tasty beverage made from pure refined protein and nutritious "
"fruit."
msgstr "정제된 단백질에 영양소 풍부한 과일을 섞어 만든, 걸쭉하고 맛 좋은 음료."

#: data\json\items\comestibles\protein.json
msgid "fortified protein shake"
msgid_plural "fortified protein shakes"
msgstr[0] "단백질 셰이크 강화주"

#. ~ Conditional name for fortified protein shake when VITAMIN matches
#. human_flesh_vitamin
#: data\json\items\comestibles\protein.json
msgid "fortified soylent green shake"
msgid_plural "fortified soylent green shakes"
msgstr[0] "소일렌트 그린 셰이크 강화주"

#. ~ Description for fortified protein shake
#: data\json\items\comestibles\protein.json
msgid ""
"A thick and tasty beverage made from pure refined protein and nutritious "
"fruit.  It has been supplemented with extra vitamins and minerals"
msgstr "정제된 단백질에 영양가가 높은 과일을 섞어 만든, 걸쭉하고 맛 좋은 음료. 비타민과 미네랄을 첨가했습니다."

#: data\json\items\comestibles\raw_fruit.json
msgid "apple"
msgid_plural "apples"
msgstr[0] "사과"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'apple'}
#: data\json\items\comestibles\raw_fruit.json
msgid "An apple a day keeps the doctor away."
msgstr "매일 사과를 먹으면 의사와 만날 일이 점점 적어진다고 합니다."

#: data\json\items\comestibles\raw_fruit.json
#: data\mods\Aftershock\items\seed.json
msgid "banana"
msgid_plural "bananas"
msgstr[0] "바나나"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'banana'}
#: data\json\items\comestibles\raw_fruit.json
msgid ""
"A long, curved yellow fruit in a peel.  Some people like using them in "
"desserts.  Those people are probably dead."
msgstr ""
"껍질에 싸인, 길고 휘어진 노란색 과일입니다. 몇몇 사람들은 후식으로 이걸 먹기를 좋아합니다. 아마도 그들은 지금은 죽었겠지요."

#: data\json\items\comestibles\raw_fruit.json
msgid "cacao pod"
msgid_plural "cacao pod"
msgstr[0] "카카오 열매"

#. ~ Description for {'str_sp': 'cacao pod'}
#: data\json\items\comestibles\raw_fruit.json
msgid ""
"The cacao fruit, scientifically known as Theobroma cacao, is the source of "
"cocoa beans used to make chocolate.  It is a tropical fruit that contains "
"cocoa beans surrounded by a sweet-tasting, white pulp.  The beans are "
"harvested, fermented, and processed to produce various chocolate products."
msgstr ""
"학명 Theobroma cacao인 카카오 열매는 초콜릿을 만드는 코코아 콩의 원천입니다. 달콤한 맛의 흰 펄프에 둘러싸인 코코아 콩이 "
"든 열대 과일입니다. 콩을 수확, 발효, 가공해 다양한 초콜릿 제품을 만듭니다."

#: data\json\items\comestibles\raw_fruit.json
#: data\mods\Aftershock\items\seed.json
msgid "orange"
msgid_plural "oranges"
msgstr[0] "오렌지"

#. ~ Description for orange
#: data\json\items\comestibles\raw_fruit.json
msgid "Sweet citrus fruit.  Also comes in juice form."
msgstr "달콤한 감귤류의 과일입니다. 주스로 만들어 먹을 수도 있습니다."

#: data\json\items\comestibles\raw_fruit.json
#: data\mods\Aftershock\items\seed.json
msgid "lemon"
msgid_plural "lemons"
msgstr[0] "레몬"

#. ~ Description for lemon
#: data\json\items\comestibles\raw_fruit.json
msgid "Very sour citrus.  Can be eaten if you really want."
msgstr "매우 시큼한 감귤류 과일입니다. 꼭 먹어야만 하겠다면 먹을 수는 있습니다."

#: data\json\items\comestibles\raw_fruit.json
msgid "blueberries"
msgid_plural "blueberries"
msgstr[0] "블루베리"

#. ~ Description for {'str_sp': 'blueberries'}
#: data\json\items\comestibles\raw_fruit.json
msgid "They're blue, but that doesn't mean they're sad."
msgstr ""
"블루베리는 파랗지만, 그렇다고 슬프다는 뜻은 아니다.\r\n"
"(역주: 'blue'에는 '우울한'이라는 의미도 있다.)"

#: data\json\items\comestibles\raw_fruit.json
msgid "strawberries"
msgid_plural "strawberries"
msgstr[0] "딸기"

#. ~ Description for {'str_sp': 'strawberries'}
#: data\json\items\comestibles\raw_fruit.json
msgid "Tasty, juicy berry.  Often found growing wild in fields."
msgstr "맛있는 과즙이 들어있는 열매. 종종 들판에서 자라나는 것을 발견할 수 있다."

#: data\json\items\comestibles\raw_fruit.json
msgid "cranberries"
msgid_plural "cranberries"
msgstr[0] "크랜베리"

#. ~ Description for {'str_sp': 'cranberries'}
#: data\json\items\comestibles\raw_fruit.json
msgid "Sour red berries.  Good for your health."
msgstr "새콤한 붉은색 열매입니다. 건강에 좋습니다."

#: data\json\items\comestibles\raw_fruit.json
msgid "raspberries"
msgid_plural "raspberries"
msgstr[0] "라즈베리"

#. ~ Description for {'str_sp': 'raspberries'}
#: data\json\items\comestibles\raw_fruit.json
msgid "A sweet red berry."
msgstr "달콤한 붉은색 열매입니다."

#: data\json\items\comestibles\raw_fruit.json
msgid "huckleberries"
msgid_plural "huckleberries"
msgstr[0] "허클베리"

#. ~ Description for {'str_sp': 'huckleberries'}
#: data\json\items\comestibles\raw_fruit.json
msgid "Huckleberries, often times confused for blueberries."
msgstr "가끔씩 불루베리와 헷갈리는 월귤나무 열매."

#: data\json\items\comestibles\raw_fruit.json
msgid "mulberries"
msgid_plural "mulberries"
msgstr[0] "오디"

#. ~ Description for {'str_sp': 'mulberries'}
#: data\json\items\comestibles\raw_fruit.json
msgid ""
"Mulberries, this red variety is unique to east North America and is "
"described to have the strongest flavor of any variety in the world."
msgstr "빨간 오디는 북미 동부 지역에서만 나타나며 세계에서 가장 풍미가 뛰어난 종으로 알려져 있습니다."

#: data\json\items\comestibles\raw_fruit.json
msgid "elderberries"
msgid_plural "elderberries"
msgstr[0] "엘더베리"

#. ~ Description for {'str_sp': 'elderberries'}
#: data\json\items\comestibles\raw_fruit.json
msgid "Elderberries, toxic when eaten raw but great when cooked."
msgstr "날것으로 먹으면 독성이 있으니 요리해 먹는 것이 좋다."

#: data\json\items\comestibles\raw_fruit.json
msgid "rose hips"
msgid_plural "rose hips"
msgstr[0] "로즈힙"

#. ~ Description for {'str_sp': 'rose hips'}
#: data\json\items\comestibles\raw_fruit.json
msgid "The fruit of a pollinated rose flower."
msgstr "수분된 장미꽃의 열매."

#: data\json\items\comestibles\raw_fruit.json
msgid "juice pulp"
msgid_plural "juice pulps"
msgstr[0] "으깬 과육"

#. ~ Description for juice pulp
#: data\json\items\comestibles\raw_fruit.json
msgid ""
"Left-over from juicing the fruit.  Not very tasty, but contains a lot of "
"healthy fiber."
msgstr "과일에서 즙을 짜내고 남은 찌꺼기. 맛은 별로지만, 건강에 좋은 식이섬유가 많이 함유되어 있다."

#: data\json\items\comestibles\raw_fruit.json
msgid "pear"
msgid_plural "pears"
msgstr[0] "배"

#. ~ Description for pear
#: data\json\items\comestibles\raw_fruit.json
msgid "A juicy, bell-shaped pear.  Yum!"
msgstr "과즙이 풍부한 종 모양의 서양배입니다. 냠!"

#: data\json\items\comestibles\raw_fruit.json
msgid "grapefruit"
msgid_plural "grapefruits"
msgstr[0] "자몽"

#. ~ Description for grapefruit
#: data\json\items\comestibles\raw_fruit.json
msgid "A citrus fruit, whose taste ranges from sour to semi-sweet."
msgstr "새콤 달콤한 감귤류 과일입니다."

#: data\json\items\comestibles\raw_fruit.json
msgid "cherries"
msgid_plural "cherries"
msgstr[0] "체리"

#. ~ Description for {'str_sp': 'cherries'}
#: data\json\items\comestibles\raw_fruit.json
msgid "A red, sweet fruit that grows in trees."
msgstr "나무에서 자라는 붉고 달콤한 과일입니다."

#: data\json\items\comestibles\raw_fruit.json
msgid "plum"
msgid_plural "plums"
msgstr[0] "자두"

#. ~ Description for plum
#: data\json\items\comestibles\raw_fruit.json
msgid ""
"A handful of large, purple plums.  Healthy and good for your digestion."
msgstr "적당히 큰 보라색 자두입니다. 몸에 좋고, 소화를 돕습니다."

#: data\json\items\comestibles\raw_fruit.json
msgid "grapes"
msgid_plural "grapes"
msgstr[0] "포도"

#. ~ Description for {'str_sp': 'grapes'}
#: data\json\items\comestibles\raw_fruit.json
msgid "A cluster of juicy grapes."
msgstr "즙이 많은 포도 한 송이."

#: data\json\items\comestibles\raw_fruit.json
#: data\mods\Aftershock\items\seed.json
msgid "pineapple"
msgid_plural "pineapples"
msgstr[0] "파인애플"

#. ~ Description for pineapple
#: data\json\items\comestibles\raw_fruit.json
msgid "A large, spiky pineapple.  A bit sour, though."
msgstr "크고, 가시난 파인애플입니다. 약간 신 맛이 납니다."

#: data\json\items\comestibles\raw_fruit.json
#: data\mods\Aftershock\items\seed.json
msgid "coconut"
msgid_plural "coconuts"
msgstr[0] "코코넛"

#. ~ Description for coconut
#: data\json\items\comestibles\raw_fruit.json
msgid "A fruit with a hard and hairy shell."
msgstr "단단하고 털이 많은 껍데기를 가진 과일입니다."

#: data\json\items\comestibles\raw_fruit.json
msgid "peach"
msgid_plural "peaches"
msgstr[0] "복숭아"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'peach', 'str_pl': 'peaches'}
#: data\json\items\comestibles\raw_fruit.json
msgid "This fruit's large pit is surrounded by its tasty flesh."
msgstr "큰 씨앗을 맛있는 과육이 감싸고 있는 과일입니다."

#: data\json\items\comestibles\raw_fruit.json
msgid "watermelon"
msgid_plural "watermelons"
msgstr[0] "수박"

#. ~ Description for watermelon
#: data\json\items\comestibles\raw_fruit.json
msgid "A fruit, bigger than your head.  It is very juicy!"
msgstr "사람의 머리보다 큰 과일입니다. 과즙이 풍부합니다!"

#: data\json\items\comestibles\raw_fruit.json
#: data\mods\Aftershock\items\seed.json
msgid "melon"
msgid_plural "melons"
msgstr[0] "멜론"

#. ~ Description for melon
#: data\json\items\comestibles\raw_fruit.json
msgid "A large and very sweet fruit."
msgstr "크고 아주 달콤한 과일입니다."

#: data\json\items\comestibles\raw_fruit.json
msgid "blackberries"
msgid_plural "blackberries"
msgstr[0] "블랙베리"

#. ~ Description for {'str_sp': 'blackberries'}
#: data\json\items\comestibles\raw_fruit.json
msgid "A darker cousin of raspberry."
msgstr "산딸기의 검은색 사촌입니다."

#: data\json\items\comestibles\raw_fruit.json
msgid "mango"
msgid_plural "mangos"
msgstr[0] "망고"

#. ~ Description for mango
#: data\json\items\comestibles\raw_fruit.json
msgid "A fleshy fruit with large pit."
msgstr "큰 씨앗을 가진, 다육질의 과일입니다."

#: data\json\items\comestibles\raw_fruit.json
msgid "pomegranate"
msgid_plural "pomegranates"
msgstr[0] "석류"

#. ~ Description for pomegranate
#: data\json\items\comestibles\raw_fruit.json
msgid "Under this pomegranate's spongy skin lies hundreds of fleshy seeds."
msgstr "스펀지 같은 과육 밑에 수백 개의 씨앗이 있는 과일입니다."

#: data\json\items\comestibles\raw_fruit.json
msgid "papaya"
msgid_plural "papayas"
msgstr[0] "파파야"

#. ~ Description for papaya
#: data\json\items\comestibles\raw_fruit.json
msgid "A very sweet and soft tropical fruit."
msgstr "아주 달콤하고 부드러운 열대 과일입니다."

#: data\json\items\comestibles\raw_fruit.json
msgid "kiwi"
msgid_plural "kiwis"
msgstr[0] "키위"

#. ~ Description for kiwi
#: data\json\items\comestibles\raw_fruit.json
msgid ""
"A large, brown and fuzzy-skinned berry.  Its delicious insides are green."
msgstr "털로 뒤덮인 갈색 껍질의 알찬 열매. 초록색 내용물이 맛있다."

#: data\json\items\comestibles\raw_fruit.json
msgid "apricots"
msgid_plural "apricots"
msgstr[0] "살구"

#. ~ Description for {'str_sp': 'apricots'}
#: data\json\items\comestibles\raw_fruit.json
msgid "A smooth-skinned fruit, related to the peach."
msgstr "부드러운 촉감의 과일로, 복숭아와 비슷한 과일입니다."

#: data\json\items\comestibles\raw_fruit.json
msgid "cholla bud"
msgid_plural "cholla buds"
msgstr[0] "초야 새싹"

#. ~ Description for cholla bud
#: data\json\items\comestibles\raw_fruit.json
msgid ""
"Edible bud of a cholla cactus, with spines removed; the candy of the Mojave "
"indigenous peoples.  Tastes similar to asparagus."
msgstr "가시를 제거한 식용 초야 선인장 새싹으로, 모하비 원주민의 사탕이었습니다. 아스파라거스 비슷한 맛입니다."

#: data\json\items\comestibles\raw_fruit.json
msgid "cactus pad"
msgid_plural "cactus pads"
msgstr[0] "선인장 잎"

#. ~ Description for cactus pad
#: data\json\items\comestibles\raw_fruit.json
msgid "An edible pad of a cactus."
msgstr "식용 선인장 잎입니다."

#: data\json\items\comestibles\raw_veggy.json
#: data\json\items\comestibles\seed.json
msgid "barley"
msgid_plural "barleys"
msgstr[0] "보리"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'barley'}
#: data\json\items\comestibles\raw_veggy.json
msgid ""
"Grainy cereal used for malting.  A staple of brewing everywhere.  It can "
"also be ground into flour."
msgstr "맥주 제조에 사용되는 거친 곡물. 양조에 필수적인 재료이며, 빻아서 가루로 만들 수도 있다."

#: data\json\items\comestibles\raw_veggy.json
#: data\json\items\comestibles\seed.json
msgid "bee balm"
msgid_plural "bee balms"
msgstr[0] "향수박하"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'bee balm'}
#: data\json\items\comestibles\raw_veggy.json
msgid ""
"A snow-white flower also known as wild bergamot.  Smells faintly of mint."
msgstr "수레박하라고도 알려진 새하얀 꽃. 희미한 민트향이 난다."

#: data\json\items\comestibles\raw_veggy.json
#: data\json\items\comestibles\seed.json
msgid "broccoli"
msgid_plural "broccoli"
msgstr[0] "브로콜리"

#. ~ Description for {'str_sp': 'broccoli'}
#: data\json\items\comestibles\raw_veggy.json
msgid "It's a bit tough, but quite delicious."
msgstr "먹기 조금 힘들지만, 꽤 맛있다."

#: data\json\items\comestibles\raw_veggy.json
#: data\json\items\comestibles\seed.json
msgid "buckwheat"
msgid_plural "buckwheat"
msgstr[0] "메밀"

#. ~ Description for {'str_sp': 'buckwheat'}
#: data\json\items\comestibles\raw_veggy.json
msgid ""
"Seeds from a wild buckwheat plant.  Not particularly good to eat in their "
"raw state, they are commonly cooked or ground into flour."
msgstr "야생 메밀에서 얻은 씨앗. 생으로 먹기보다 요리하거나 가루로 빻아서 먹는다."

#: data\json\items\comestibles\raw_veggy.json
#: data\json\items\comestibles\seed.json
msgid "cabbage"
msgid_plural "cabbages"
msgstr[0] "양배추"

#. ~ Description for cabbage
#: data\json\items\comestibles\raw_veggy.json
msgid "Crisp white cabbage."
msgstr "아삭한 양배추."

#: data\json\items\comestibles\raw_veggy.json
msgid "grape leaves"
msgid_plural "grape leaves"
msgstr[0] "포도 잎"

#. ~ Description for {'str_sp': 'grape leaves'}
#: data\json\items\comestibles\raw_veggy.json
msgid ""
"Edible leaves of a grape vine.  Typically used in salads or as food "
"wrapping."
msgstr "식용 포도덩굴 잎입니다. 보통 샐러드나 음식 포장에 쓰입니다."

#: data\json\items\comestibles\raw_veggy.json
msgid "spinach"
msgid_plural "spinach"
msgstr[0] "시금치"

#. ~ Description for {'str_sp': 'spinach'}
#: data\json\items\comestibles\raw_veggy.json
msgid "A bunch of spinach leaves."
msgstr "시금치 잎 한 다발입니다."

#: data\json\items\comestibles\raw_veggy.json
#: data\json\items\comestibles\seed.json
msgid "carrot"
msgid_plural "carrots"
msgstr[0] "당근"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'carrot'}
#: data\json\items\comestibles\raw_veggy.json
msgid "A healthy root vegetable.  Rich in vitamin A!"
msgstr "건강에 좋은 뿌리 채소. 비타민 A가 풍부하다!"

#: data\json\items\comestibles\raw_veggy.json
msgid "cattail rhizome"
msgid_plural "cattail rhizomes"
msgstr[0] "부들 뿌리"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'cattail rhizome'}
#: data\json\items\comestibles\raw_veggy.json
msgid ""
"A stout branching rhizome from a cattail plant.  Its crisp white flesh is "
"very starchy and fibrous, but you really ought to cook it before you attempt"
" to eat it."
msgstr "부들에서 채취한 뿌리 줄기. 싱싱한 하얀 줄기는 아삭하고 탄수화물, 섬유질이 풍부하지만, 먹기 전에 조리를 해야 한다."

#: data\json\items\comestibles\raw_veggy.json
msgid "cattail stalk"
msgid_plural "cattail stalks"
msgstr[0] "부들 줄기"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'cattail stalk'}
#: data\json\items\comestibles\raw_veggy.json
msgid ""
"A stiff green stalk from a cattail plant.  It is starchy and fibrous, but it"
" would be much better if you cooked it."
msgstr "부들에서 채취한 단단한 녹색 줄기. 녹말과 섬유질이 많으며, 조리하면 더욱 먹기 좋아진다."

#: data\json\items\comestibles\raw_veggy.json
#: data\json\items\comestibles\seed.json
msgid "celery"
msgid_plural "celerys"
msgstr[0] "셀러리"

#. ~ Description for celery
#: data\json\items\comestibles\raw_veggy.json
msgid "Neither tasty nor very nutritious, but it goes well with salad."
msgstr "맛도 없고 영양가도 없지만, 샐러드와 잘 어울립니다."

#: data\json\items\comestibles\raw_veggy.json
#: data\json\items\comestibles\seed.json
#: data\json\items\comestibles\veggy_dishes.json
msgid "corn"
msgid_plural "corn"
msgstr[0] "옥수수"

#. ~ Description for {'str_sp': 'corn'}
#: data\json\items\comestibles\raw_veggy.json
msgid "Delicious golden kernels."
msgstr "맛있는 황금색 알갱이들."

#: data\json\items\comestibles\raw_veggy.json
msgid "cotton boll"
msgid_plural "cotton bolls"
msgstr[0] "목화다래"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'cotton boll'}
#: data\json\items\comestibles\raw_veggy.json
msgid ""
"A tough protective capsule bulging with densely packed fibers and seeds, "
"this cotton boll can be processed into usable material with the right tools."
msgstr "튼튼한 껍데기 안에 섬유와 씨가 들어있다. 적절한 도구를 사용해 유용한 재료로 바꿀 수 있다."

#: data\json\items\comestibles\raw_veggy.json
#: data\json\items\comestibles\seed.json
msgid "chili pepper"
msgid_plural "chili peppers"
msgstr[0] "고추"

#. ~ Description for chili pepper
#: data\json\items\comestibles\raw_veggy.json
msgid "Spicy chili pepper."
msgstr "매운 고추다."

#: data\json\items\comestibles\raw_veggy.json
#: data\json\items\comestibles\seed.json
msgid "cucumber"
msgid_plural "cucumbers"
msgstr[0] "오이"

#. ~ Description for cucumber
#: data\json\items\comestibles\raw_veggy.json
msgid "Comes from the gourd family.  Not tasty but very juicy."
msgstr "박과에 속합니다. 맛은 없지만 수분이 매우 풍부합니다."

#: data\json\items\comestibles\raw_veggy.json
msgid "dahlia root"
msgid_plural "dahlia roots"
msgstr[0] "달리아 뿌리"

#. ~ Description for dahlia root
#: data\json\items\comestibles\raw_veggy.json
msgid ""
"The large, tuberous root of a dahlia flower.  It smells spicy, but is too "
"starchy to eat without cooking."
msgstr "달리아 꽃의 크고 덩이줄기 뿌리입니다. 매콤한 냄새가 나지만, 조리 없이는 전분이 너무 많아 먹을 수 없습니다."

#: data\json\items\comestibles\raw_veggy.json
#: data\json\items\comestibles\seed.json
msgid "salsify"
msgid_plural "salsify"
msgstr[0] "살시파이"

#. ~ Description for {'str_sp': 'salsify'}
#: data\json\items\comestibles\raw_veggy.json
msgid ""
"An herb with a small purple flower.  The roots are nutritious, but tough and"
" bland until cooked."
msgstr "작은 보라 꽃이 있는 약초입니다. 뿌리는 영양가 있지만, 조리 전까진 질기고 싱겁습니다."

#. ~ Description for {'str_sp': 'chicory'}
#: data\json\items\comestibles\raw_veggy.json
msgid ""
"A modest blue flower.  The flower's roots are very bitter and not meant to "
"be eaten raw."
msgstr "수수한 파란 꽃입니다. 꽃의 뿌리는 매우 쓰고 날로 먹도록 된 게 아닙니다."

#: data\json\items\comestibles\raw_veggy.json
#: data\json\items\comestibles\seed.json
msgid "wild root"
msgid_plural "wild roots"
msgstr[0] "야생 뿌리"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'wild root'}
#: data\json\items\comestibles\raw_veggy.json
msgid ""
"A weed with a cluster of tiny white flowers.  These are often wild carrots, "
"but beware of poisonous lookalikes."
msgstr "작은 흰 꽃 다발이 있는 잡초입니다. 종종 야생 당근이지만, 독성 유사종을 조심하세요."

#: data\json\items\comestibles\raw_veggy.json
#: data\json\items\comestibles\seed.json
msgid "dogbane"
msgid_plural "dogbanes"
msgstr[0] "개정향풀"

#. ~ Description for dogbane
#: data\json\items\comestibles\raw_veggy.json
msgid ""
"A stalk of dogbane.  It has very fibrous stems and is mildly poisonous."
msgstr "개정향풀 줄기. 섬유질이 풍부하고 약한 독성을 가지고 있다."

#: data\json\items\comestibles\raw_veggy.json
msgid "garlic bulb"
msgid_plural "garlic bulbs"
msgstr[0] "통마늘"

#. ~ Description for garlic bulb
#: data\json\items\comestibles\raw_veggy.json
msgid ""
"A pungent garlic bulb.  Popular as a seasoning for its strong flavor.  Can "
"be disassembled to cloves."
msgstr "자극적인 향이 나는 마늘 구근. 강한 풍미 덕분에 양념으로 인기가 좋습니다. 쪽으로 분리할 수 있습니다."

#: data\json\items\comestibles\raw_veggy.json
msgid "hops flower"
msgid_plural "hops flowers"
msgstr[0] "홉 꽃"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'hops flower'}
#: data\json\items\comestibles\raw_veggy.json
msgid "A cluster of small cone-like flowers, indispensable for brewing beer."
msgstr "작은 옥수수처럼 생긴 꽃 한 송이. 맥주를 양조할 때 반드시 필요하다."

#: data\json\items\comestibles\raw_veggy.json
msgid "horseradish root"
msgid_plural "horseradish roots"
msgstr[0] "호스래디시 뿌리"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'horseradish root'}
#: data\json\items\comestibles\raw_veggy.json
msgid ""
"Large white tapered root of a horseradish plant.  Way too spicy in this "
"form, but can be used for making condiments."
msgstr "호스래디시 식물의 크고 흰 가늘어지는 뿌리입니다. 이 형태로는 너무 맵지만, 양념을 만드는 데 쓸 수 있습니다."

#: data\json\items\comestibles\raw_veggy.json
#: data\json\items\comestibles\seed.json
msgid "lettuce"
msgid_plural "lettuces"
msgstr[0] "양상추"

#. ~ Description for lettuce
#: data\json\items\comestibles\raw_veggy.json
msgid "A crisp head of iceberg lettuce."
msgstr "아삭거리는 양상추."

#: data\json\items\comestibles\raw_veggy.json
#: data\json\items\comestibles\seed.json
msgid "mugwort"
msgid_plural "mugworts"
msgstr[0] "쑥"

#. ~ Description for mugwort
#: data\json\items\comestibles\raw_veggy.json
msgid "A stalk of mugwort.  Smells wonderful."
msgstr "쑥 줄기. 냄새가 독하다."

#: data\json\items\comestibles\raw_veggy.json
#: data\json\items\comestibles\seed.json
msgid "onion"
msgid_plural "onions"
msgstr[0] "양파"

#. ~ Description for onion
#: data\json\items\comestibles\raw_veggy.json
msgid ""
"An aromatic onion used in cooking.  Cutting these up can make your eyes "
"sting!"
msgstr "요리에 쓰이는 향기로운 양파. 자르면 눈물이 날 수도 있습니다!"

#: data\json\items\comestibles\raw_veggy.json
msgid "fungal fluid sac"
msgid_plural "fungal fluid sacs"
msgstr[0] "진균 체액 주머니"

#. ~ Description for fungal fluid sac
#: data\json\items\comestibles\raw_veggy.json
msgid ""
"A fluid bladder from a fungus based lifeform.  Not very nutritious, but fine"
" to eat anyway."
msgstr "진균 기반 생명체의 체액 주머니입니다. 영양가는 별로 없지만 어쨌든 먹어도 괜찮습니다."

#: data\json\items\comestibles\raw_veggy.json
msgid "raw popcorn"
msgid_plural "raw popcorn"
msgstr[0] "날 팝콘 옥수수"

#. ~ Description for {'str_sp': 'raw popcorn'}
#: data\json\items\comestibles\raw_veggy.json
msgid ""
"A special variety of corn which could be used for making popcorn, after it's"
" dried.  Unlike normal corn, it's not sweet and is more dry."
msgstr "마른 뒤 팝콘을 만드는 데 쓸 수 있는 특수 옥수수 품종입니다. 일반 옥수수와 달리 달지 않고 더 건조합니다."

#: data\json\items\comestibles\raw_veggy.json
msgid "raw potato"
msgid_plural "raw potatoes"
msgstr[0] "생 감자"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'raw potato', 'str_pl': 'raw potatoes'}
#: data\json\items\comestibles\raw_veggy.json
msgid "Mildly toxic and not very tasty raw.  When cooked, it is delicious."
msgstr "가벼운 독성이 있고, 생으로는 그다지 맛이 없습니다. 요리하면 맛있어집니다."

#: data\json\items\comestibles\raw_veggy.json
#: data\json\items\comestibles\seed.json
msgid "pumpkin"
msgid_plural "pumpkins"
msgstr[0] "호박"

#. ~ Description for pumpkin
#: data\json\items\comestibles\raw_veggy.json
msgid ""
"A large vegetable, about the size of your head.  Not very tasty raw, but is "
"great for cooking."
msgstr "커다란 채소. 대략 당신의 머리만 합니다. 생으로는 별로지만, 요리해 먹으면 아주 맛있습니다."

#: data\json\items\comestibles\raw_veggy.json
msgid "horseradish greens"
msgid_plural "horseradish greens"
msgstr[0] "호스래디시 잎"

#. ~ Description for {'str_sp': 'horseradish greens'}
#: data\json\items\comestibles\raw_veggy.json
msgid ""
"Leaves of a horseradish plant with a sharp, bitter and peppery taste.  "
"They're edible, but not commonly eaten."
msgstr "날카롭고 쓰며 후추 같은 맛이 나는 호스래디시 식물의 잎입니다. 먹을 수 있지만 흔히 먹진 않습니다."

#: data\json\items\comestibles\raw_veggy.json
msgid "dandelions"
msgid_plural "dandelions"
msgstr[0] "민들레"

#. ~ Description for {'str_sp': 'dandelions'}
#: data\json\items\comestibles\raw_veggy.json
msgid ""
"A collection of freshly picked yellow dandelions.  In their current raw "
"state they are quite bitter."
msgstr "신선할 때 수확된 민들레. 생으로 먹기엔 매우 쓰다."

#: data\json\items\comestibles\raw_veggy.json
msgid "burdocks"
msgid_plural "burdocks"
msgstr[0] "우엉"

#. ~ Description for {'str_sp': 'burdocks'}
#: data\json\items\comestibles\raw_veggy.json
msgid "Burdock, a bitter thistle-like vegetable.  Can be eaten raw or cooked."
msgstr "쓴 엉겅퀴 같은 채소, 우엉입니다. 날로 또는 조리해 먹을 수 있습니다."

#: data\json\items\comestibles\raw_veggy.json
#: data\json\items\comestibles\seed.json
msgid "rhubarb"
msgid_plural "rhubarbs"
msgstr[0] "대황"

#. ~ Description for rhubarb
#: data\json\items\comestibles\raw_veggy.json
msgid "Sour stems of the rhubarb plant, often used in baking pies."
msgstr "대황 식물의 줄기로, 파이를 구울 때 쓰입니다."

#: data\json\items\comestibles\raw_veggy.json
#: data\json\items\comestibles\seed.json
msgid "sugar beet"
msgid_plural "sugar beets"
msgstr[0] "사탕무"

#. ~ Description for sugar beet
#: data\json\items\comestibles\raw_veggy.json
msgid ""
"This fleshy root is ripe and flowing with sugars; just takes some processing"
" to extract them."
msgstr "당분이 함유된 두꺼운 뿌리식물. 몇몇 공정을 거치면 설탕을 추출할 수 있다."

#: data\json\items\comestibles\raw_veggy.json
msgid "tea leaf"
msgid_plural "tea leaves"
msgstr[0] "찻잎"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'tea leaf', 'str_pl': 'tea leaves'}
#: data\json\items\comestibles\raw_veggy.json
msgid ""
"Dried leaves of a tropical plant.  You can boil them into tea, or you can "
"just eat them raw.  They aren't too filling though."
msgstr ""
"말린 열대 식물의 잎입니다. 끓여서 차로 먹을 수도 있고, 생으로 먹을 수도 있습니다. 어느 쪽이건 배를 채워주지는 못합니다."

#: data\json\items\comestibles\raw_veggy.json
msgid "coca leaf"
msgid_plural "coca leaves"
msgstr[0] "코카 잎"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'coca leaf', 'str_pl': 'coca leaves'}
#: data\json\items\comestibles\raw_veggy.json
msgid ""
"Coca leaves.  Have a long history of medicinal and culinary uses, and can "
"produce a mild high when chewed.  You can boil them into tea or you can just"
" eat them raw.  Can cause addiction if consumed in large quantities."
msgstr ""
"코카 잎입니다. 약용과 요리용으로 오랜 역사가 있고, 씹으면 가벼운 기분 고양이 올 수 있습니다. 차로 끓이거나 그냥 날로 먹을 수 "
"있습니다. 대량 섭취하면 중독될 수 있습니다."

#: data\json\items\comestibles\raw_veggy.json
#: data\json\items\comestibles\seed.json
msgid "tomato"
msgid_plural "tomatoes"
msgstr[0] "토마토"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'tomato', 'str_pl': 'tomatoes'}
#: data\json\items\comestibles\raw_veggy.json
msgid ""
"Juicy red tomato.  It gained popularity in Italy after being brought back "
"from the New World."
msgstr "과즙 많은 빨간 토마토. 신대륙에서 이탈리아로 넘어오면서 인기를 끌기 시작했다."

#: data\json\items\comestibles\raw_veggy.json
msgid "plant marrow"
msgid_plural "plant marrows"
msgstr[0] "식물 알맹이"

#. ~ Description for plant marrow
#: data\json\items\comestibles\raw_veggy.json
msgid "A nutrient rich chunk of plant matter, could be eaten raw or cooked."
msgstr "영양소가 풍부한 식물 덩어리입니다. 생으로 먹을 수 있고, 요리해서도 먹을 수 있습니다."

#: data\json\items\comestibles\raw_veggy.json
msgid "alien fungus chunk"
msgid_plural "alien fungus chunks"
msgstr[0] "외계 진균 덩어리"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'alien fungus chunk'}
#: data\json\items\comestibles\raw_veggy.json
msgid ""
"This is a chunk of fungal matter from some sort of alien mushroom creature."
"  Eating unfamiliar mushrooms is a bad idea."
msgstr "일종의 외계 버섯 생물에서 나온 진균 물질 덩어리입니다. 익숙지 않은 버섯을 먹는 건 나쁜 생각입니다."

#: data\json\items\comestibles\raw_veggy.json
msgid "wild vegetables"
msgid_plural "wild vegetables"
msgstr[0] "산나물"

#. ~ Description for {'str_sp': 'wild vegetables'}
#: data\json\items\comestibles\raw_veggy.json
msgid ""
"An assortment of edible-looking wild plants.  Most are quite bitter-tasting."
"  Some are inedible until cooked."
msgstr "먹을 수 있을 것처럼 생긴 야생 식물. 대부분 쓴 맛만 납니다. 어떤 것은 요리하지 않으면 먹을 수 없습니다."

#: data\json\items\comestibles\raw_veggy.json
#: data\json\items\comestibles\seed.json
msgid "zucchini"
msgid_plural "zucchinis"
msgstr[0] "주키니"

#. ~ Description for zucchini
#: data\json\items\comestibles\raw_veggy.json
msgid "A tasty summer squash."
msgstr "여름에 나오는 맛있는 호박."

#: data\json\items\comestibles\raw_veggy.json
#: data\json\items\comestibles\seed.json
msgid "canola"
msgid_plural "canolas"
msgstr[0] "카놀라"

#. ~ Description for canola
#: data\json\items\comestibles\raw_veggy.json
msgid "A pretty stalk of canola.  Its seeds can be pressed into oil."
msgstr "카놀라 줄기. 기름을 짜낼 수 있다."

#: data\json\items\comestibles\raw_veggy.json
msgid "raw beans"
msgid_plural "raw beans"
msgstr[0] "생 콩"

#. ~ Description for {'str_sp': 'raw beans'}
#: data\json\items\comestibles\raw_veggy.json
msgid ""
"Raw, uncooked beans.  They are mildly toxic in this form, but you could cook"
" them to make them tasty."
msgstr "날것의 조리되지 않은 콩입니다. 이 형태로는 약간 독성이 있지만, 조리하면 맛있게 만들 수 있습니다."

#: data\json\items\comestibles\raw_veggy.json
msgid "raw lentils"
msgid_plural "raw lentils"
msgstr[0] "날 렌틸콩"

#. ~ Description for {'str_sp': 'raw lentils'}
#: data\json\items\comestibles\raw_veggy.json
msgid "Raw, uncooked lentils.  They could be cooked."
msgstr "날것의 조리되지 않은 렌틸콩입니다. 조리할 수 있습니다."

#: data\json\items\comestibles\raw_veggy.json
msgid "fiddleheads"
msgid_plural "fiddleheads"
msgstr[0] "고사리 순"

#. ~ Description for {'str_sp': 'fiddleheads'}
#: data\json\items\comestibles\raw_veggy.json
msgid ""
"A handful of immature fern fronds, still curled up like the head of a "
"fiddle.  Delicious when cooked, but consuming raw can cause food poisoning."
msgstr "바이올린 머리처럼 말려 있는 미성숙 고사리 잎 한 줌입니다. 조리하면 맛있지만, 날로 먹으면 식중독이 올 수 있습니다."

#: data\json\items\comestibles\raw_veggy.json
msgid "rice bran"
msgid_plural "rice brans"
msgstr[0] "쌀겨"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'rice bran'}
#: data\json\items\comestibles\raw_veggy.json
msgid ""
"The leftover outer layer of rice seeds, this vegetable matter is quite "
"nutritionally dense and makes for a good cooking oil."
msgstr "쌀 씨앗의 남은 겉층으로, 이 식물성 물질은 영양 밀도가 높고 좋은 식용유가 됩니다."

#: data\json\items\comestibles\raw_veggy.json
msgid "aquatic greens"
msgid_plural "aquatic greens"
msgstr[0] "수생 채소"

#. ~ Description for {'str_sp': 'aquatic greens'}
#: data\json\items\comestibles\raw_veggy.json
msgid ""
"Shoots and leaves from underwater plants, such as hornwort or pondweed.  A "
"bit like raw seaweed."
msgstr "북미산새나 몰 줄풀 같은 수중 식물의 새싹과 잎입니다. 날 해초 비슷합니다."

#: data\json\items\comestibles\sandwich.json
msgid "GENERIC SANDWICH"
msgid_plural "GENERIC SANDWICHES"
msgstr[0] "일반 샌드위치"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'GENERIC SANDWICH', 'str_pl': 'GENERIC
#. SANDWICHES'}
#: data\json\items\comestibles\sandwich.json
msgid ""
"If you can see this, you shouldn't be able to.  This is to solve dumb copy-"
"from issues."
msgstr "이게 보인다면, 보여선 안 되는 겁니다. 멍청한 copy-from 문제를 해결하기 위한 것입니다."

#: data\json\items\comestibles\sandwich.json
msgid "deluxe sandwich"
msgid_plural "deluxe sandwiches"
msgstr[0] "디럭스 샌드위치"

#. ~ Conditional name for {'str': 'deluxe sandwich', 'str_pl': 'deluxe
#. sandwiches'} when COMPONENT_ID matches mutant
#: data\json\items\comestibles\sandwich.json
msgid "\"deluxe\" sandwich"
msgid_plural "\"deluxe\" sandwiches"
msgstr[0] "\"디럭스\" 샌드위치"

#. ~ Conditional name for {'str': 'deluxe sandwich', 'str_pl': 'deluxe
#. sandwiches'} when FLAG matches CANNIBALISM
#: data\json\items\comestibles\sandwich.json
msgid "slob deluxe sandwich"
msgid_plural "slob deluxe sandwiches"
msgstr[0] "잡식 디럭스 샌드위치"

#. ~ Conditional name for {'str': 'deluxe sandwich', 'str_pl': 'deluxe
#. sandwiches'} when COMPONENT_ID matches seasoning_salt
#. ~ Conditional name for {'str': 'dairy-free deluxe sandwich', 'str_pl':
#. 'dairy-free deluxe sandwiches'} when COMPONENT_ID matches seasoning_salt
#: data\json\items\comestibles\sandwich.json
#, c-format
msgid "%s with seasoned salt"
msgid_plural "%s with seasoned salts"
msgstr[0] "시즈닝 소금을 얹은 %s"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'deluxe sandwich', 'str_pl': 'deluxe sandwiches'}
#: data\json\items\comestibles\sandwich.json
msgid ""
"A sandwich of meat, vegetables, and cheese with condiments.  Tasty and "
"nutritious!"
msgstr "고기, 야채, 치즈를 넣어 만든 샌드위치. 맛있고 영양이 풍부합니다."

#: data\json\items\comestibles\sandwich.json
msgid "grilled cheese sandwich"
msgid_plural "grilled cheese sandwiches"
msgstr[0] "구운 치즈 샌드위치"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'grilled cheese sandwich', 'str_pl': 'grilled
#. cheese sandwiches'}
#: data\json\items\comestibles\sandwich.json
msgid ""
"A delicious grilled cheese sandwich, because everything is better with "
"melted cheese."
msgstr "맛있게 구운 치즈 샌드위치. 녹인 치즈와 함께면 뭐든간에 더 나아진다."

#: data\json\items\comestibles\sandwich.json
#: data\mods\Tolerate_This\comestibles.json
msgid "cheese sandwich"
msgid_plural "cheese sandwiches"
msgstr[0] "치즈 샌드위치"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'cheese sandwich', 'str_pl': 'cheese sandwiches'}
#: data\json\items\comestibles\sandwich.json
#: data\mods\Tolerate_This\comestibles.json
msgid "A simple cheese sandwich."
msgstr "간단한 치즈 샌드위치."

